:: ---- gr.recall.policy.del (preference) ------------------------------
::P|gr.recall.policy.del|REVIEW|REVIEW|REVIEW|REVIEW|REVIEW|
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.001|WINDOWS RECALL, COTE RESTAURATION
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.002|
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.003|  Ce que c est    : Les trois valeurs de strategie WindowsAI et le type de
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.004|                    demarrage de WSAIFabricSvc, abordes depuis le menu de
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.005|                    restauration. Recall capture regulierement l'ecran et
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.006|                    l'indexe pour rendre l'activite passee consultable ;
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.007|                    il n'existe que sur materiel Copilot+ et s'y active
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.008|                    volontairement.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.009|
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.010|  Effet reel      : Supprime les trois valeurs de strategie et remet
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.011|                    WSAIFabricSvc en demarrage a la demande : Recall
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.012|                    redevient activable la ou le materiel le permet.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.013|
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.014|  Gain            : Aucun sur du materiel ordinaire : il n'y a pas de
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.015|                    Recall a restaurer. Sur une machine Copilot+, vous
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.016|                    retrouvez la recherche dans la chronologie, si vous la
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.017|                    voulez vraiment.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.018|
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.019|  Cout            : Sur Copilot+, les captures d'ecran redeviennent
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.020|                    possibles une fois que vous les activez. Partout
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.021|                    ailleurs, rien ne change dans un sens comme dans
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.022|                    l'autre.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.023|
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.024|  Defaut Windows  : Les trois valeurs absentes, et le service laisse tel
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.025|                    que l'image l'a livre.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.026|
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.027|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.028|    DisableAIDataAnalysis=1 :
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.029|        Recall n'a pas le droit d'enregistrer d'instantanes.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.030|        L'interrupteur Recall dans Parametres est grise avec une mention
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.031|        de strategie, et la chaine de capture ne demarre jamais.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.032|    DisableAIDataAnalysis=0 :
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.033|        Ce n'est pas le defaut : c'est un "autorise par strategie"
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.034|        explicite, donc un troisieme etat. L'interrupteur reste grise
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.035|        comme gere, simplement dans le sens permissif. N'ecrivez jamais
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.036|        cette valeur pour annuler le blocage : supprimez-la.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.037|    AllowRecallEnablement=0 :
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.038|        Recall ne peut plus etre active du tout, meme par un
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.039|        administrateur qui le souhaite. C'est la plus dure des deux
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.040|        strategies : DisableAIDataAnalysis stoppe les captures, celle-ci
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.041|        retire l'option.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.042|    AllowRecallEnablement=1 :
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.043|        "Peut etre active" explicite. La encore un troisieme etat, pas la
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.044|        condition d'origine.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.045|    DELETE               : L'etat d'origine des trois valeurs : absentes.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.046|                           Sur materiel Copilot+, Recall se comporte alors
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.047|                           comme prevu - inactif tant que l'utilisateur ne
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.048|                           l'active pas, instantanes stockes en local et
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.049|                           proteges par Windows Hello. Sur materiel non
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.050|                           Copilot+, absent et 1 sont indiscernables : il
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.051|                           n'y a rien avec quoi capturer.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.052|    WSAIFabricSvc=disabled :
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.053|        sc config start= disabled. Le service qui heberge la couche IA
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.054|        locale ne peut plus etre demarre par quoi que ce soit, y compris
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.055|        la chaine Recall. Sur une machine ou le service n'existe pas, la
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.056|        commande echoue et ne change rien.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.057|    WSAIFabricSvc=demand : Demarrage a la demande : le service reste
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.058|                           inerte tant que la chaine IA ne le reclame pas.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.059|                           C'est ce qu'ecrit la branche de restauration,
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.060|                           et c'est une supposition raisonnable plus qu'un
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.061|                           defaut verifie.
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.062|    SKIP                 : Laisse le type de demarrage du service tel
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.063|                           quel. La reponse honnete quand on ne connait
::T|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.064|                           pas la valeur d'origine.
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Meme tableau que la carte de configuration,
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.002|                         puisqu'il s'agit des memes trois valeurs. Gaming,
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.003|                         serveur et portable bloquent : l'ecriture ne
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.004|                         coute rien nulle part, et sur la seule categorie
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.005|                         de machine ou Recall existe vraiment - un
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.006|                         portable Copilot+ - la capture continue plus
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.007|                         l'indexation sur NPU representent une vraie
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.008|                         charge de fond, raison pour laquelle le profil
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.009|                         oriente autonomie n'est pas l'exception ici.
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.010|                         L'exception, c'est la bureautique, et
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.011|                         volontairement : la premisse de ce profil est que
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.012|                         les fonctions restent actives, Recall est deja
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.013|                         optionnel et chiffre localement, et le bloquer
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.014|                         par strategie grise un interrupteur qu'un membre
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.015|                         de la famille peut legitimement vouloir. La
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.016|                         reponse Windows est la suppression, puisque
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.017|                         l'absence est le vrai defaut et qu'ecrire 0
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.018|                         serait un troisieme etat.
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.019|
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.020|  Problemes connus : Sur materiel non Copilot+, les appels sc sur
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.021|                     WSAIFabricSvc echouent en silence et le journal
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.022|                     declare quand meme l'etape faite : c'est un defaut de
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.023|                     rapport du script, pas un probleme Windows.
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.024|
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.025|  Non verifie (en)  : I could not verify the shipped start type of
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.026|                      WSAIFabricSvc, so the restore branch writing start=
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.027|                      demand is an assumption, not a known default - that
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.028|                      is why the profile table leaves the service alone
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.029|                      rather than asserting a value. I also could not
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.030|                      confirm that the service exists at all outside
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.031|                      Copilot+ builds; on a machine without it both sc
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.032|                      calls fail and the >nul 2>&1 hides that, so the log
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.033|                      claims a change that never happened.
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.034|
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.035|  Cible           : reg delete
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.036|                    "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsAI"
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.037|                    /v "DisableAIDataAnalysis" /f ; reg delete same key /v
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.038|                    "AllowRecallEnablement" /f ; reg delete
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.039|                    "HKCU\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsAI"
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.040|                    /v "DisableAIDataAnalysis" /f ; sc config
::X|FR|gr.recall.policy.del.041|                    WSAIFabricSvc start= demand (OPTY.bat lines 1637-1640)
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.001|WINDOWS RECALL, RESTORE SIDE
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.002|
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.003|  What it is      : The three WindowsAI policy values and the
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.004|                    WSAIFabricSvc start type, approached from the restore
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.005|                    menu. Recall periodically captures the screen and
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.006|                    indexes it so past activity becomes searchable; it
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.007|                    exists only on Copilot+ hardware and is opt-in there.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.008|
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.009|  Actual effect   : Deletes the three policy values and sets WSAIFabricSvc
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.010|                    back to demand, so Recall becomes available to opt
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.011|                    into where the hardware supports it.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.012|
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.013|  Gain            : None on ordinary hardware - there is no Recall to
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.014|                    restore. On a Copilot+ machine you get the timeline
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.015|                    search back if you actually want it.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.016|
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.017|  Cost            : On Copilot+, screen snapshots become possible again
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.018|                    once you opt in. On everything else, nothing changes
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.019|                    in either direction.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.020|
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.021|  Windows default : All three values absent; the service left at whatever
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.022|                    the image shipped.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.023|
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.024|  Possible values:
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.025|    DisableAIDataAnalysis=1 :
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.026|        Recall may not save snapshots. The Recall toggle in Settings is
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.027|        greyed with a policy note and the snapshot pipeline never starts.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.028|    DisableAIDataAnalysis=0 :
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.029|        Not the default - it is an explicit "allowed by policy", a third
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.030|        state. It still greys the toggle as managed, just in the
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.031|        permissive direction. Never write this to undo the block; delete
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.032|        the value instead.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.033|    AllowRecallEnablement=0 :
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.034|        Recall cannot be turned on at all, even by an administrator who
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.035|        wants it. This is the harder of the two policies -
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.036|        DisableAIDataAnalysis stops the snapshots, this one removes the
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.037|        option.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.038|    AllowRecallEnablement=1 :
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.039|        Explicit "may be enabled". A third state again, not the shipped
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.040|        condition.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.041|    DELETE               : The shipped state for all three values: absent.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.042|                           On Copilot+ hardware Recall then behaves as
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.043|                           designed - off until the user opts in,
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.044|                           snapshots stored locally and gated behind
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.045|                           Windows Hello. On non-Copilot+ hardware absent
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.046|                           and 1 are indistinguishable, because there is
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.047|                           nothing to snapshot with.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.048|    WSAIFabricSvc=disabled :
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.049|        sc config start= disabled. The service that hosts the on-device AI
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.050|        fabric cannot be started by anything, including the Recall
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.051|        pipeline. On a machine where the service does not exist, this
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.052|        command fails and changes nothing.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.053|    WSAIFabricSvc=demand : Start on demand: the service sits idle until
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.054|                           the AI pipeline asks for it. This is what the
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.055|                           restore branch writes, and it is a reasonable
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.056|                           guess rather than a verified default.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.057|    SKIP                 : Leave the service start type exactly as found.
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.058|                           The honest answer when the shipped value is not
::T|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.059|                           known.
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.001|  Why these profiles : Same table as the setup card, because it is the
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.002|                       same three values. Gaming, server and laptop block:
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.003|                       the write costs nothing anywhere, and on the one
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.004|                       machine class where Recall is real - a Copilot+
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.005|                       laptop - continuous snapshotting plus NPU indexing
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.006|                       is a genuine background load, which is why the
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.007|                       battery-first profile is not the exception here.
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.008|                       Office is the exception, and deliberately so: that
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.009|                       profile's whole premise is features on, Recall is
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.010|                       already opt-in and locally encrypted, and blocking
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.011|                       it by policy greys a Settings toggle a family
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.012|                       member might legitimately want. The Windows answer
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.013|                       is delete, since absence is the real default and
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.014|                       writing 0 would be a third state.
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.015|
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.016|  Known problems  : On non-Copilot+ hardware the sc calls against
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.017|                    WSAIFabricSvc fail silently and the log still reports
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.018|                    the step as done - a reporting defect in the script,
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.019|                    not a Windows problem.
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.020|
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.021|  Unverified      : I could not verify the shipped start type of
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.022|                    WSAIFabricSvc, so the restore branch writing start=
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.023|                    demand is an assumption, not a known default - that is
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.024|                    why the profile table leaves the service alone rather
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.025|                    than asserting a value. I also could not confirm that
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.026|                    the service exists at all outside Copilot+ builds; on
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.027|                    a machine without it both sc calls fail and the >nul
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.028|                    2>&1 hides that, so the log claims a change that never
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.029|                    happened.
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.030|
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.031|  Target          : reg delete
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.032|                    "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsAI"
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.033|                    /v "DisableAIDataAnalysis" /f ; reg delete same key /v
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.034|                    "AllowRecallEnablement" /f ; reg delete
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.035|                    "HKCU\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsAI"
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.036|                    /v "DisableAIDataAnalysis" /f ; sc config
::X|EN|gr.recall.policy.del.037|                    WSAIFabricSvc start= demand (OPTY.bat lines 1637-1640)
