::P|gr.spotlight.policy.del|1|1|DELETE|1|DELETE|
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.001|WINDOWS SPOTLIGHT, COTE RESTAURATION
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.002|
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.003|  Ce que c est    : La strategie machine qui coupe d'un bloc les images
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.004|                    tournantes de l'ecran de verrouillage et du bureau,
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.005|                    ainsi que les conseils affiches par-dessus.
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.006|
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.007|  Effet reel      : Supprime la valeur : les images Spotlight et le theme
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.008|                    Spotlight du bureau refonctionnent.
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.009|
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.010|  Gain            : Vous retrouvez les photos tournantes, si vous les
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.011|                    aimiez, et la page Personnalisation cesse d'afficher
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.012|                    une mention de strategie.
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.013|
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.014|  Cout            : Les surcouches de conseils et leurs liens
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.015|                    promotionnels reviennent avec les images : c'est une
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.016|                    seule fonction, pas deux.
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.017|
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.018|  Defaut Windows  : Absente, Spotlight actif.
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.019|
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.020|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.021|    1                    : Toute la famille Spotlight est coupee : plus de
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.022|                           photos tournantes sur l'ecran de verrouillage,
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.023|                           plus de theme Spotlight du bureau, plus de
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.024|                           surcouches de conseils ni de liens
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.025|                           promotionnels "vous aimez cette image".
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.026|                           L'option Windows Spotlight disparait de la
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.027|                           liste deroulante de Personnalisation au lieu
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.028|                           d'y rester simplement non selectionnee, et
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.029|                           comme il s'agit d'une strategie HKLM, elle
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.030|                           s'applique a tous les comptes de la machine.
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.031|    0                    : Un "Spotlight autorise par strategie"
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.032|                           explicite. Troisieme etat, pas la condition
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.033|                           d'origine ; Personnalisation reste marquee
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.034|                           comme geree.
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.035|    DELETE               : Absente, l'etat d'origine. Spotlight est
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.036|                           disponible et chaque utilisateur le choisit, ou
::T|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.037|                           non, dans Personnalisation.
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Gaming, serveur et portable ecrivent 1 ;
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.002|                         bureautique et la reponse Windows suppriment.
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.003|                         Soyons clairs sur la taille du gain : il n'y a
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.004|                         ici aucun gain CPU ni memoire, et le
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.005|                         telechargement se limite a quelques images sur
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.006|                         une rotation lente. L'argument honnete pour 1,
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.007|                         c'est que vous ne voulez pas de liens
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.008|                         promotionnels sur votre ecran de verrouillage et
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.009|                         que vous mettez votre propre image de toute
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.010|                         facon. Cette valeur a en revanche un cout que les
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.011|                         autres reglages de confidentialite n'ont pas :
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.012|                         etant une strategie HKLM, elle marque
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.013|                         Personnalisation comme geree par votre
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.014|                         organisation pour tous les comptes, exactement la
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.015|                         banniere que ce script se refuse a provoquer
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.016|                         ailleurs. La bureautique supprime autant pour
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.017|                         cette raison que pour les photos. Et si vous avez
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.018|                         repondu 1 sur la carte des applications
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.019|                         sponsorisees, celle-ci est peut-etre deja
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.020|                         redondante.
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.021|
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.022|  Problemes connus : Avec la strategie a 1, Windows Spotlight disparait de
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.023|                     la liste Personnalisation > Ecran de verrouillage et
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.024|                     Parametres affiche sur cette page une mention "gere
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.025|                     par votre organisation" pour tous les utilisateurs de
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.026|                     la machine.
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.027|
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.028|  Non verifie (en)  : I did not measure how much Spotlight actually
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.029|                      downloads. It is a handful of images on a slow
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.030|                      rotation, so calling it a bandwidth saving is
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.031|                      generous; treat the network argument as small rather
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.032|                      than as a headline. Whether
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.033|                      DisableWindowsConsumerFeatures=1 already suppresses
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.034|                      Spotlight on 25H2, making this value redundant, is
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.035|                      also unverified.
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.036|
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.037|  Cible           : reg delete "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\C
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.038|                    loudContent" /v "DisableWindowsSpotlightFeatures" /f
::X|FR|gr.spotlight.policy.del.039|                    (OPTY.bat line 1686)
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.001|WINDOWS SPOTLIGHT, RESTORE SIDE
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.002|
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.003|  What it is      : The machine-wide policy that switches off the rotating
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.004|                    lock-screen and desktop imagery together with the tips
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.005|                    shown on it.
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.006|
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.007|  Actual effect   : Deletes the value, so the Spotlight pictures and the
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.008|                    Spotlight desktop theme work again.
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.009|
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.010|  Gain            : You get the rotating photographs back, if you liked
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.011|                    them, and the Personalization page stops showing a
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.012|                    policy marking.
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.013|
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.014|  Cost            : The tip overlays and their promotional links come back
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.015|                    with the pictures - they are one feature, not two.
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.016|
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.017|  Windows default : Absent, Spotlight on.
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.018|
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.019|  Possible values:
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.020|    1                    : The whole Spotlight family is off: no rotating
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.021|                           lock-screen photographs, no Spotlight desktop
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.022|                           theme, no tip overlays and no "like what you
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.023|                           see" promotional links. The Windows Spotlight
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.024|                           option disappears from the Personalization
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.025|                           dropdown rather than being merely unselected,
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.026|                           and because this is an HKLM policy it applies
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.027|                           to every account on the machine.
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.028|    0                    : An explicit "Spotlight allowed by policy". A
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.029|                           third state, not the shipped condition; it
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.030|                           still marks Personalization as managed.
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.031|    DELETE               : Absent, the shipped state. Spotlight is
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.032|                           available and each user picks it, or not, in
::T|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.033|                           Personalization.
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.001|  Why these profiles : Gaming, server and laptop set 1; office and the
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.002|                       Windows answer delete. Be clear about the size of
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.003|                       the win, though: there is no CPU or RAM gain here
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.004|                       at all, and the download is a few images on a slow
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.005|                       rotation, so the honest case for 1 is that you do
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.006|                       not want promotional links on your lock screen and
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.007|                       you set your own image anyway. It also carries a
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.008|                       cost the other privacy knobs do not - because it is
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.009|                       an HKLM policy it stamps Personalization as managed
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.010|                       by your organization for every account, which is
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.011|                       exactly the banner this script otherwise refuses to
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.012|                       cause. Office deletes for that reason as much as
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.013|                       for the photographs. If you also answered 1 on the
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.014|                       sponsored-apps card, this one may already be
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.015|                       redundant.
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.016|
::X|EN|gr.spotlight.policy.del.017|  Known problems  : With the policy at 1, Windows Spotlight vanishes from
