:: ---- db.recall.off (preference) -------------------------------------
::P|db.recall.off|REVIEW|REVIEW|REVIEW|REVIEW|REVIEW|
::T|FR|db.recall.off.001|BLOQUER WINDOWS RECALL
::T|FR|db.recall.off.002|
::T|FR|db.recall.off.003|  Ce que c est    : Recall capture regulierement l'ecran et l'indexe pour
::T|FR|db.recall.off.004|                    rendre l'activite passee consultable. Il n'existe que
::T|FR|db.recall.off.005|                    sur materiel Copilot+, ou il est optionnel, stocke son
::T|FR|db.recall.off.006|                    index en local et protege l'acces par Windows Hello.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.007|                    Les trois valeurs de strategie le refusent au niveau
::T|FR|db.recall.off.008|                    machine et utilisateur ; l'appel au service arrete le
::T|FR|db.recall.off.009|                    composant qui ferait le travail.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.010|
::T|FR|db.recall.off.011|  Effet reel      : Ecrit DisableAIDataAnalysis=1 sous HKLM et HKCU,
::T|FR|db.recall.off.012|                    AllowRecallEnablement=0 sous HKLM, puis arrete et
::T|FR|db.recall.off.013|                    desactive WSAIFabricSvc.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.014|
::T|FR|db.recall.off.015|  Gain            : Sur un PC Copilot+, vrai gain de confidentialite et
::T|FR|db.recall.off.016|                    vraie charge en moins : aucun historique d'ecran n'est
::T|FR|db.recall.off.017|                    construit et le service de couche IA ne tourne pas.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.018|                    Partout ailleurs, aucun gain mesurable d'aucune sorte,
::T|FR|db.recall.off.019|                    puisque Recall n'est pas la : les ecritures ne sont
::T|FR|db.recall.off.020|                    qu'une assurance bon marche au cas ou la machine
::T|FR|db.recall.off.021|                    serait mise a niveau ou la fonction elargie plus tard.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.022|                    N'attendez de ceci ni une image par seconde ni un watt
::T|FR|db.recall.off.023|                    sur un poste ordinaire.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.024|
::T|FR|db.recall.off.025|  Cout            : Vous perdez la recherche dans la chronologie Recall
::T|FR|db.recall.off.026|                    sur le materiel qui en dispose. Rien d'autre ne lit
::T|FR|db.recall.off.027|                    ces cles.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.028|
::T|FR|db.recall.off.029|  Defaut Windows  : Les trois absentes ; Recall optionnel et reserve au
::T|FR|db.recall.off.030|                    Copilot+.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.031|
::T|FR|db.recall.off.032|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|db.recall.off.033|    DisableAIDataAnalysis=1 :
::T|FR|db.recall.off.034|        Recall n'a pas le droit de capturer ni d'analyser d'instantanes.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.035|        Ecrite au niveau machine et utilisateur pour qu'un reglage par
::T|FR|db.recall.off.036|        utilisateur ne puisse pas la contourner. L'interrupteur dans
::T|FR|db.recall.off.037|        Parametres se grise avec une mention de strategie.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.038|    DisableAIDataAnalysis=0 :
::T|FR|db.recall.off.039|        Explicitement autorise par strategie : troisieme etat, pas le
::T|FR|db.recall.off.040|        defaut, et l'interrupteur reste marque comme gere. Pour annuler le
::T|FR|db.recall.off.041|        blocage, supprimez la valeur au lieu d'ecrire 0.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.042|    AllowRecallEnablement=0 :
::T|FR|db.recall.off.043|        Recall ne peut plus etre active du tout. Plus fort que la valeur
::T|FR|db.recall.off.044|        precedente : l'une arrete les captures, celle-ci retire le choix.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.045|    AllowRecallEnablement=1 :
::T|FR|db.recall.off.046|        Explicitement autorise. La encore un troisieme etat.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.047|    DELETE               : Absente : l'etat d'origine des trois. Recall
::T|FR|db.recall.off.048|                           reste inactif tant qu'un utilisateur ne
::T|FR|db.recall.off.049|                           l'active pas, et uniquement sur materiel
::T|FR|db.recall.off.050|                           Copilot+.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.051|    WSAIFabricSvc=disabled :
::T|FR|db.recall.off.052|        Le service de couche IA locale ne peut plus demarrer, quel que
::T|FR|db.recall.off.053|        soit l'appelant. Sur materiel Copilot+, c'est ce qui supprime
::T|FR|db.recall.off.054|        reellement le cout resident ; ailleurs, la commande echoue et rien
::T|FR|db.recall.off.055|        ne change.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.056|    WSAIFabricSvc=demand : Ne demarre que lorsque la chaine IA le reclame.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.057|                           Si Recall est bloque par strategie, plus rien
::T|FR|db.recall.off.058|                           ne le reclame : a la demande devient donc
::T|FR|db.recall.off.059|                           fonctionnellement proche de desactive une fois
::T|FR|db.recall.off.060|                           les strategies en place.
::T|FR|db.recall.off.061|    SKIP                 : Laisse le type de demarrage tel quel. La
::T|FR|db.recall.off.062|                           reponse honnete tant que la valeur d'origine
::T|FR|db.recall.off.063|                           n'est pas verifiee.
::X|FR|db.recall.off.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Trois profils bloquent, deux laissent l'etat
::X|FR|db.recall.off.002|                         d'origine, et le partage ne tient pas a une
::X|FR|db.recall.off.003|                         preference de confidentialite mais a la vocation
::X|FR|db.recall.off.004|                         de chaque profil. Gaming et serveur bloquent
::X|FR|db.recall.off.005|                         parce que l'ecriture ne coute rien nulle part et
::X|FR|db.recall.off.006|                         qu'aucune des deux machines n'a l'usage d'un
::X|FR|db.recall.off.007|                         index d'ecran. Le portable bloque pour une raison
::X|FR|db.recall.off.008|                         reellement mesurable sur la seule categorie de
::X|FR|db.recall.off.009|                         materiel ou Recall existe : sur un portable
::X|FR|db.recall.off.010|                         Copilot+, la capture continue et l'indexation sur
::X|FR|db.recall.off.011|                         NPU sont une vraie charge de fond, et le profil
::X|FR|db.recall.off.012|                         oriente autonomie ne la tolere pas. La
::X|FR|db.recall.off.013|                         bureautique est l'exception assumee : sa premisse
::X|FR|db.recall.off.014|                         est que les fonctions restent actives, Recall est
::X|FR|db.recall.off.015|                         deja optionnel et chiffre localement, et le
::X|FR|db.recall.off.016|                         bloquer par strategie grise un interrupteur qu'un
::X|FR|db.recall.off.017|                         membre du foyer peut legitimement vouloir
::X|FR|db.recall.off.018|                         essayer. Windows supprime, parce que l'absence
::X|FR|db.recall.off.019|                         est le vrai defaut et qu'ecrire 0 serait un
::X|FR|db.recall.off.020|                         troisieme etat, pas une restauration.
::X|FR|db.recall.off.021|
::X|FR|db.recall.off.022|  Problemes connus : Sur du materiel depourvu des composants IA Copilot+,
::X|FR|db.recall.off.023|                     les deux commandes sc echouent et le script
::X|FR|db.recall.off.024|                     journalise malgre tout l'etape comme appliquee.
::X|FR|db.recall.off.025|
::X|FR|db.recall.off.026|  Non verifie (en)  : WSAIFabricSvc appears to ship only with the Copilot+
::X|FR|db.recall.off.027|                      AI components; on hardware without them both sc
::X|FR|db.recall.off.028|                      calls fail and the redirection hides it, so the log
::X|FR|db.recall.off.029|                      reports a step that did not happen. I also did not
::X|FR|db.recall.off.030|                      verify the service's shipped start type, which is
::X|FR|db.recall.off.031|                      why no profile asserts one on the way back.
::X|FR|db.recall.off.032|
::X|FR|db.recall.off.033|  Cible           : reg add
::X|FR|db.recall.off.034|                    "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsAI"
::X|FR|db.recall.off.035|                    /v "DisableAIDataAnalysis" /t REG_DWORD /d 1 /f ; reg
::X|FR|db.recall.off.036|                    add same key /v "AllowRecallEnablement" /t REG_DWORD
::X|FR|db.recall.off.037|                    /d 0 /f ; reg add
::X|FR|db.recall.off.038|                    "HKCU\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsAI"
::X|FR|db.recall.off.039|                    /v "DisableAIDataAnalysis" /t REG_DWORD /d 1 /f ; sc
::X|FR|db.recall.off.040|                    stop WSAIFabricSvc ; sc config WSAIFabricSvc start=
::X|FR|db.recall.off.041|                    disabled (OPTY.bat lines 1710-1714)
::T|EN|db.recall.off.001|BLOCK WINDOWS RECALL
::T|EN|db.recall.off.002|
::T|EN|db.recall.off.003|  What it is      : Recall periodically snapshots the screen and indexes
::T|EN|db.recall.off.004|                    it so past activity becomes searchable. It exists only
::T|EN|db.recall.off.005|                    on Copilot+ hardware, where it is opt-in, stores its
::T|EN|db.recall.off.006|                    index locally and gates access behind Windows Hello.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.007|                    The three policy values here refuse it at machine and
::T|EN|db.recall.off.008|                    user level; the service call stops the component that
::T|EN|db.recall.off.009|                    would do the work.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.010|
::T|EN|db.recall.off.011|  Actual effect   : Writes DisableAIDataAnalysis=1 at HKLM and HKCU,
::T|EN|db.recall.off.012|                    AllowRecallEnablement=0 at HKLM, then stops and
::T|EN|db.recall.off.013|                    disables WSAIFabricSvc.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.014|
::T|EN|db.recall.off.015|  Gain            : On a Copilot+ PC this is a real privacy gain and a
::T|EN|db.recall.off.016|                    real load removed: no screen history is built and the
::T|EN|db.recall.off.017|                    AI fabric service does not run. On everything else
::T|EN|db.recall.off.018|                    there is no measurable gain of any kind, because
::T|EN|db.recall.off.019|                    Recall is not present - the writes are cheap insurance
::T|EN|db.recall.off.020|                    against the machine later being upgraded or the
::T|EN|db.recall.off.021|                    feature being pushed wider, and nothing more. Do not
::T|EN|db.recall.off.022|                    expect a frame or a watt from this on a normal
::T|EN|db.recall.off.023|                    desktop.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.024|
::T|EN|db.recall.off.025|  Cost            : You lose Recall's timeline search on hardware that has
::T|EN|db.recall.off.026|                    it. Nothing else reads these keys.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.027|
::T|EN|db.recall.off.028|  Windows default : All three absent; Recall opt-in on Copilot+ only.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.029|
::T|EN|db.recall.off.030|  Possible values:
::T|EN|db.recall.off.031|    DisableAIDataAnalysis=1 :
::T|EN|db.recall.off.032|        Recall may not take or analyse snapshots. Written at machine and
::T|EN|db.recall.off.033|        user level so a per-user override cannot re-enable it. The
::T|EN|db.recall.off.034|        Settings toggle greys out with a policy note.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.035|    DisableAIDataAnalysis=0 :
::T|EN|db.recall.off.036|        Explicitly permitted by policy - a third state, not the default,
::T|EN|db.recall.off.037|        and it keeps the toggle marked as managed. To undo the block,
::T|EN|db.recall.off.038|        delete the value instead of writing 0.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.039|    AllowRecallEnablement=0 :
::T|EN|db.recall.off.040|        Recall cannot be switched on at all. Stronger than the value
::T|EN|db.recall.off.041|        above: one stops the snapshots, this one removes the choice.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.042|    AllowRecallEnablement=1 :
::T|EN|db.recall.off.043|        Explicitly allowed. A third state again.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.044|    DELETE               : Absent - the shipped state for all three.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.045|                           Recall stays off until a user opts in, and only
::T|EN|db.recall.off.046|                           on Copilot+ hardware.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.047|    WSAIFabricSvc=disabled :
::T|EN|db.recall.off.048|        The on-device AI fabric service cannot start, for any caller. On
::T|EN|db.recall.off.049|        Copilot+ hardware this is what actually removes the resident cost;
::T|EN|db.recall.off.050|        on other hardware the command fails and nothing changes.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.051|    WSAIFabricSvc=demand : Starts only when the AI pipeline asks. If
::T|EN|db.recall.off.052|                           Recall is blocked by policy, nothing asks - so
::T|EN|db.recall.off.053|                           demand is functionally close to disabled once
::T|EN|db.recall.off.054|                           the policies are in place.
::T|EN|db.recall.off.055|    SKIP                 : Leave the start type as found. The honest
::T|EN|db.recall.off.056|                           answer while the shipped value is unverified.
::X|EN|db.recall.off.001|  Why these profiles : Three profiles block and two leave it stock, and
::X|EN|db.recall.off.002|                       the split is not about privacy taste but about what
::X|EN|db.recall.off.003|                       the profile is for. Gaming and server block because
::X|EN|db.recall.off.004|                       the write costs nothing anywhere and neither
::X|EN|db.recall.off.005|                       machine has any use for a screen index. Laptop
::X|EN|db.recall.off.006|                       blocks for a reason that is actually measurable on
::X|EN|db.recall.off.007|                       the one hardware class where Recall exists:
::X|EN|db.recall.off.008|                       continuous snapshotting plus NPU indexing is a
::X|EN|db.recall.off.009|                       genuine background load on a Copilot+ laptop, and
::X|EN|db.recall.off.010|                       the battery-first profile does not tolerate that.
::X|EN|db.recall.off.011|                       Office is the deliberate exception - its premise is
::X|EN|db.recall.off.012|                       that features stay on, Recall is already opt-in and
::X|EN|db.recall.off.013|                       locally encrypted, and blocking it by policy greys
::X|EN|db.recall.off.014|                       a Settings toggle that a household member might
::X|EN|db.recall.off.015|                       legitimately want to try. Windows deletes, because
::X|EN|db.recall.off.016|                       absence is the true default and writing 0 would be
::X|EN|db.recall.off.017|                       a third state, not a restore.
::X|EN|db.recall.off.018|
::X|EN|db.recall.off.019|  Known problems  : On hardware without the Copilot+ AI components the two
::X|EN|db.recall.off.020|                    sc commands fail and the script still logs the step as
::X|EN|db.recall.off.021|                    applied.
::X|EN|db.recall.off.022|
::X|EN|db.recall.off.023|  Unverified      : WSAIFabricSvc appears to ship only with the Copilot+
::X|EN|db.recall.off.024|                    AI components; on hardware without them both sc calls
::X|EN|db.recall.off.025|                    fail and the redirection hides it, so the log reports
::X|EN|db.recall.off.026|                    a step that did not happen. I also did not verify the
::X|EN|db.recall.off.027|                    service's shipped start type, which is why no profile
::X|EN|db.recall.off.028|                    asserts one on the way back.
::X|EN|db.recall.off.029|
::X|EN|db.recall.off.030|  Target          : reg add
::X|EN|db.recall.off.031|                    "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsAI"
::X|EN|db.recall.off.032|                    /v "DisableAIDataAnalysis" /t REG_DWORD /d 1 /f ; reg
::X|EN|db.recall.off.033|                    add same key /v "AllowRecallEnablement" /t REG_DWORD
::X|EN|db.recall.off.034|                    /d 0 /f ; reg add
::X|EN|db.recall.off.035|                    "HKCU\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsAI"
::X|EN|db.recall.off.036|                    /v "DisableAIDataAnalysis" /t REG_DWORD /d 1 /f ; sc
::X|EN|db.recall.off.037|                    stop WSAIFabricSvc ; sc config WSAIFabricSvc start=
::X|EN|db.recall.off.038|                    disabled (OPTY.bat lines 1710-1714)
