:: ---- db.consumerfeatures.off (preference) ---------------------------
::P|db.consumerfeatures.off|1|1|1|1|DELETE|
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.001|STOPPER L'INSTALLATION SILENCIEUSE D'APPLICATIONS SPONSORISEES
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.002|
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.003|  Ce que c est    : DisableWindowsConsumerFeatures, une strategie machine
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.004|                    qui empeche Windows d'installer d'office des
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.005|                    applications et des jeux promotionnels dans les
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.006|                    profils utilisateur.
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.007|
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.008|  Effet reel      : Ecrit 1 : les nouveaux profils ne recoivent plus les
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.009|                    vignettes sponsorisees du Store.
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.010|
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.011|  Gain            : Un menu Demarrer propre sur les nouveaux profils et
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.012|                    aucun telechargement surprise en connexion limitee.
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.013|                    C'est un gain de bande passante et de place disque,
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.014|                    pas de CPU : il n'y a aucun processus a arreter ici.
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.015|
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.016|  Cout            : Rien de notable la ou la strategie est respectee. Sur
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.017|                    Famille, n'attendez aucun effet, et lisez la remarque
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.018|                    Spotlight ci-dessous.
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.019|
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.020|  Defaut Windows  : Absente, installation sponsorisee autorisee.
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.021|
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.022|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.023|    1                    : Windows arrete les experiences consommateur
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.024|                           pilotees par le cloud : plus de vignettes
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.025|                           d'applications et de jeux sponsorises
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.026|                           installees dans les profils nouvellement crees,
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.027|                           plus d'entrees promotionnelles surgissant
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.028|                           seules dans Demarrer. Cela bloque le canal de
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.029|                           livraison pour toute la machine ; cela ne
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.030|                           desinstalle rien de ce qui est deja present.
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.031|    0                    : Explicitement autorise. Troisieme etat, pas la
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.032|                           condition d'origine : pour revenir en arriere,
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.033|                           supprimez au lieu d'ecrire 0.
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.034|    DELETE               : Absente, l'etat d'origine. L'installation
::T|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.035|                           d'applications sponsorisees est autorisee.
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Quatre lignes identiques, et c'est la verite
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.002|                         plutot qu'un trou dans le tableau : un
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.003|                         telechargement d'application non sollicite
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.004|                         derange autant une machine de jeu, un serveur, un
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.005|                         PC familial et un portable, et la strategie
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.006|                         n'impose a aucun d'eux de cout d'execution a
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.007|                         mettre en balance. La bureautique n'est pas une
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.008|                         exception : des vignettes promotionnelles ne sont
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.009|                         pas une fonction que l'on perd. Seule la reponse
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.010|                         Windows supprime. Une reserve a connaitre avant
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.011|                         de compter dessus : la valeur
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.012|                         SilentInstalledAppsEnabled, par utilisateur, sur
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.013|                         la carte des suggestions, fait le meme travail
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.014|                         sans etre reservee a certaines editions - sur
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.015|                         Famille, ou sur toute version ou cette strategie
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.016|                         est ignoree, c'est elle qui porte le resultat.
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.017|
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.018|  Problemes connus : Rapporte mais non verifie : avec cette valeur a 1,
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.019|                     les images Windows Spotlight de l'ecran de
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.020|                     verrouillage cessent de tourner et retombent sur
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.021|                     l'image fixe par defaut. Si votre ecran de
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.022|                     verrouillage devient uni apres coup, c'est la raison,
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.023|                     pas un cache d'images casse.
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.024|
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.025|  Non verifie (en)  : Microsoft's ADMX has documented this policy as
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.026|                      Enterprise and Education only since Windows 10 1803.
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.027|                      It is widely reported to still work on Pro and I
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.028|                      have no evidence to the contrary, but I did not
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.029|                      verify it on 25H2 - so "yes on Pro for everyone"
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.030|                      overstated what is known. On Home, expect it to be
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.031|                      ignored. I am also fairly confident, but did not
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.032|                      verify, that 1 suppresses the Windows Spotlight
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.033|                      lock-screen imagery as a side effect.
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.034|
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.035|  Cible           : reg add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\Clou
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.036|                    dContent" /v "DisableWindowsConsumerFeatures" /t
::X|FR|db.consumerfeatures.off.037|                    REG_DWORD /d 1 /f (OPTY.bat line 1721)
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.001|STOP SILENT INSTALLS OF SPONSORED APPS
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.002|
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.003|  What it is      : DisableWindowsConsumerFeatures, a machine-wide policy
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.004|                    that blocks Windows from provisioning promotional apps
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.005|                    and games into user profiles.
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.006|
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.007|  Actual effect   : Writes 1, so new profiles do not receive the sponsored
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.008|                    Store tiles.
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.009|
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.010|  Gain            : A clean Start menu on new profiles, and no surprise
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.011|                    downloads on a metered connection. It is a bandwidth
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.012|                    and disk gain, not a CPU one - there is no process
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.013|                    here to stop.
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.014|
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.015|  Cost            : None worth mentioning where the policy is honoured. On
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.016|                    Home expect no effect at all, and see the Spotlight
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.017|                    note below.
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.018|
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.019|  Windows default : Absent, sponsored provisioning allowed.
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.020|
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.021|  Possible values:
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.022|    1                    : Windows stops the cloud-driven consumer
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.023|                           experiences: no sponsored app and game tiles
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.024|                           provisioned into newly created profiles, no
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.025|                           promotional Start entries appearing on their
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.026|                           own. It blocks the delivery path machine-wide;
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.027|                           it uninstalls nothing that is already there.
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.028|    0                    : Explicitly allowed. A third state, not the
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.029|                           shipped condition; delete rather than write 0
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.030|                           to go back.
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.031|    DELETE               : Absent, the shipped state. Sponsored
::T|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.032|                           provisioning permitted.
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.001|  Why these profiles : Four identical rows, and that is the truth rather
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.002|                       than a gap in the table: an unrequested app
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.003|                       download is unwelcome on a gaming rig, a server, a
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.004|                       family PC and a laptop in exactly the same way, and
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.005|                       the policy imposes no runtime cost on any of them
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.006|                       to trade off against. Office is not an exception
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.007|                       here - promotional tiles are not a feature anyone
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.008|                       loses. Only the Windows answer deletes. One caveat
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.009|                       worth knowing before you rely on this: the per-user
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.010|                       SilentInstalledAppsEnabled value on the suggestions
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.011|                       card does the same job and is not edition-gated, so
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.012|                       on Home or on any build where this policy is
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.013|                       ignored, that is the one carrying the weight.
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.014|
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.015|  Known problems  : Reported but unverified: with this at 1, Windows
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.016|                    Spotlight lock-screen images stop rotating and fall
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.017|                    back to the static default. If your lock screen goes
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.018|                    plain after running this, that is why, not a broken
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.019|                    image cache.
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.020|
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.021|  Unverified      : Microsoft's ADMX has documented this policy as
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.022|                    Enterprise and Education only since Windows 10 1803.
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.023|                    It is widely reported to still work on Pro and I have
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.024|                    no evidence to the contrary, but I did not verify it
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.025|                    on 25H2 - so "yes on Pro for everyone" overstated what
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.026|                    is known. On Home, expect it to be ignored. I am also
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.027|                    fairly confident, but did not verify, that 1
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.028|                    suppresses the Windows Spotlight lock-screen imagery
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.029|                    as a side effect.
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.030|
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.031|  Target          : reg add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\Clou
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.032|                    dContent" /v "DisableWindowsConsumerFeatures" /t
::X|EN|db.consumerfeatures.off.033|                    REG_DWORD /d 1 /f (OPTY.bat line 1721)
