:: ---- db.advertisingid.off (preference) ------------------------------
::P|db.advertisingid.off|0|0|0|0|1|
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.001|DESACTIVER L'IDENTIFIANT DE PUBLICITE
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.002|
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.003|  Ce que c est    : Un identifiant reinitialisable, propre a
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.004|                    l'utilisateur, que les applications du Store lisent
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.005|                    via l'API publicitaire de Windows pour cibler la
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.006|                    publicite.
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.007|
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.008|  Effet reel      : Ecrit 0 pour l'utilisateur courant : l'API ne renvoie
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.009|                    plus rien d'exploitable.
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.010|
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.011|  Gain            : Les publicites des applications du Store cessent de
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.012|                    viser un profil construit a partir de votre activite.
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.013|                    C'est tout le gain : aucun gain mesurable en vitesse,
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.014|                    en memoire ou en autonomie, puisque rien ne tourne
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.015|                    dans un cas comme dans l'autre.
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.016|
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.017|  Cout            : Vous ne verrez pas moins de pubs, seulement des pubs
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.018|                    moins pertinentes. Rien ne casse.
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.019|
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.020|  Defaut Windows  : 1, presente et activee.
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.021|
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.022|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.023|    1                    : Les applications obtiennent un veritable
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.024|                           identifiant publicitaire via l'API publicitaire
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.025|                           de Windows : une cle stable, propre a
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.026|                           l'utilisateur, qui leur permet de relier votre
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.027|                           activite entre applications et entre sessions.
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.028|                           C'est ce que contient un profil neuf.
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.029|    0                    : L'API renvoie un identifiant vide. Les
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.030|                           applications perdent la cle fournie par le
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.031|                           systeme ; elles peuvent toujours afficher des
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.032|                           pubs et se fabriquer leurs propres
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.033|                           identifiants. Aucune difference de CPU, de
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.034|                           memoire ou de reseau dans un sens comme dans
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.035|                           l'autre : c'est un interrupteur de ciblage, pas
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.036|                           de performance.
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.037|    DELETE               : Absente, la valeur se comporte exactement comme
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.038|                           1 : la supprimer ne permet donc pas de la
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.039|                           desactiver. Les deux sens de ce reglage
::T|FR|db.advertisingid.off.040|                           ecrivent par consequent une valeur explicite.
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Quatre profils ecrivent 0, et il n'y a entre eux
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.002|                         aucune difference honnete a signaler : la latence
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.003|                         en jeu, le debit d'un serveur et l'autonomie d'un
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.004|                         portable sont totalement indifferents a cette
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.005|                         valeur. La seule question posee est de savoir si
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.006|                         l'on veut que le systeme distribue une cle de
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.007|                         suivi stable, et sur une machine qui vous
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.008|                         appartient la reponse est non. La bureautique ne
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.009|                         beneficie pas ici de son exemption habituelle
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.010|                         "fonctions actives", parce que le ciblage
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.011|                         publicitaire n'est pas une fonction que
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.012|                         l'utilisateur perd. Seule la ligne Windows ecrit
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.013|                         1, et remarquez qu'elle doit l'ecrire : l'absence
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.014|                         vaut activation, donc impossible de s'en sortir
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.015|                         par une suppression.
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.016|
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.017|  Cible           : reg add "HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersio
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.018|                    n\AdvertisingInfo" /v "Enabled" /t REG_DWORD /d 0 /f
::X|FR|db.advertisingid.off.019|                    (OPTY.bat line 1729)
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.001|TURN OFF THE ADVERTISING ID
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.002|
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.003|  What it is      : A resettable per-user identifier that Store apps read
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.004|                    through the Windows Advertising API to key
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.005|                    personalised advertising.
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.006|
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.007|  Actual effect   : Writes 0 for the current user, so the API returns
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.008|                    nothing usable.
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.009|
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.010|  Gain            : Ads in Store apps stop being aimed at a profile built
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.011|                    from your activity. That is the whole gain: no
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.012|                    measurable gain in speed, memory or battery, because
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.013|                    nothing is running either way.
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.014|
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.015|  Cost            : You will not see fewer ads, only less relevant ones.
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.016|                    Nothing breaks.
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.017|
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.018|  Windows default : 1, present and enabled.
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.019|
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.020|  Possible values:
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.021|    1                    : Apps get a real advertising ID from the Windows
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.022|                           Advertising API - a stable per-user key they
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.023|                           can use to link your activity across apps and
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.024|                           sessions. This is what a fresh profile ships
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.025|                           with.
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.026|    0                    : The API hands back an empty identifier. Apps
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.027|                           lose the OS-provided key; they can still show
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.028|                           ads and can still build their own identifiers.
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.029|                           No CPU, memory or network difference either way
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.030|                           - this is a targeting switch, not a performance
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.031|                           one.
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.032|    DELETE               : Absent behaves exactly as 1, so deleting cannot
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.033|                           be used to switch it off. Both directions of
::T|EN|db.advertisingid.off.034|                           this setting therefore write an explicit value.
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.001|  Why these profiles : Four profiles write 0 and there is no honest
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.002|                       difference between them to report - gaming latency,
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.003|                       server throughput and laptop battery are all
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.004|                       completely indifferent to this value, so the only
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.005|                       question anyone is answering is whether they want
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.006|                       the OS handing out a stable tracking key, and on a
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.007|                       machine you own the answer is no. Office does not
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.008|                       get its usual features-on exemption here, because
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.009|                       ad targeting is not a feature a user loses. Only
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.010|                       the Windows row writes 1, and note that it has to
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.011|                       write it: absence means enabled, so there is no
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.012|                       delete-your-way-out on this one.
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.013|
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.014|  Target          : reg add "HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersio
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.015|                    n\AdvertisingInfo" /v "Enabled" /t REG_DWORD /d 0 /f
::X|EN|db.advertisingid.off.016|                    (OPTY.bat line 1729)
