::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.001|TURN OFF SUGGESTIONS, TIPS AND SILENT APP INSTALLS
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.002|
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.003|  What it is      : Eight ContentDeliveryManager values for the current
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.004|                    user: three Settings suggestion surfaces, the Start
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.005|                    menu suggestions, the tips toasts, the lock-screen
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.006|                    text overlay, and the two governing automatic app
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.007|                    delivery.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.008|
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.009|  Actual effect   : Writes 0 to all eight under HKCU.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.010|
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.011|  Gain            : Be precise about which one earns its place.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.012|                    SilentInstalledAppsEnabled is the real gain -
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.013|                    promotional apps stop appearing on their own, which is
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.014|                    bandwidth and disk you keep. The other seven remove
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.015|                    banners and toasts and nothing else: no process stops,
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.016|                    no service stops, and there is no measurable CPU, RAM
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.017|                    or boot gain from any of them. Lists that count them
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.018|                    as eight optimisations are counting wrong.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.019|
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.020|  Cost            : No more Settings suggestions or lock-screen tips. On a
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.021|                    first Windows 11 machine those hints are genuinely
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.022|                    useful to some people.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.023|
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.024|  Windows default : Present with 1, suggestions on.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.025|
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.026|  Possible values:
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.027|    SilentInstalledAppsEnabled=0 :
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.028|        The one with teeth. Windows stops downloading and installing
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.029|        promoted apps into your profile on its own. At 1 it can do so at
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.030|        any moment - real bandwidth, real disk, no prompt.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.031|    PreInstalledAppsEnabled=0 :
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.032|        Stops the OEM and Microsoft preinstalled-app provisioning from
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.033|        running for this profile. Governs what a newly created profile
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.034|        receives; does not uninstall anything.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.035|    SystemPaneSuggestionsEnabled=0 :
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.036|        Removes the occasional suggestion entries in the Start menu.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.037|        Cosmetic: no process, no download, nothing measurable.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.038|    SubscribedContent-338389Enabled=0 :
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.039|        Turns off the tips-and-suggestions toasts. Notifications only, no
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.040|        measurable gain.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.041|    SubscribedContent-338393Enabled=0 :
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.042|        Removes suggested content from a Settings page. A banner, nothing
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.043|        more.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.044|    SubscribedContent-353694Enabled=0 :
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.045|        Removes suggested content from a second Settings surface.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.046|    SubscribedContent-353696Enabled=0 :
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.047|        Removes suggested content from a third Settings surface.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.048|    RotatingLockScreenOverlayEnabled=0 :
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.049|        Removes the tip or fun-fact text and its promotional link drawn
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.050|        over the Spotlight lock-screen picture. The picture itself still
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.051|        rotates; that is the separate Spotlight policy.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.052|    1                    : For any of the eight: feature on. What the
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.053|                           values hold once ContentDeliveryManager has
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.054|                           created them.
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.055|    DELETE               : Absent behaves as enabled for all eight - so
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.056|                           deleting is only ever a restore, never a way to
::T|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.057|                           switch something off.
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.001|  Why these profiles : Gaming, server and laptop take all eight to 0 -
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.002|                       none of them wants a banner, a toast or an
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.003|                       unrequested download, and none of them pays
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.004|                       anything for the change. Office is split on purpose
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.005|                       rather than answered all-or-nothing: a family PC
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.006|                       should still block unrequested installs, so the two
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.007|                       delivery values go to 0 there, but it is also the
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.008|                       machine where a new user gets real value from the
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.009|                       built-in hints, so the six cosmetic ones stay at
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.010|                       their default. Windows writes 1 across the board,
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.011|                       which is where they ship.
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.012|
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.013|  Unverified      : The mapping of the numeric SubscribedContent IDs to
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.014|                    specific Settings surfaces comes from community
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.015|                    documentation rather than Microsoft, and the IDs have
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.016|                    been observed to change between builds - so a card
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.017|                    that names an exact page for each number is claiming
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.018|                    more than is known. On a fresh profile some of the
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.019|                    eight may not exist until the surface is first
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.020|                    rendered; absent behaves as enabled, so this changes
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.021|                    nothing functionally but the report should not say it
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.022|                    restored something that was never there.
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.023|
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.024|  Target          : reg add on HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVers
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.025|                    ion\ContentDeliveryManager, REG_DWORD 0, for
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.026|                    SubscribedContent-338393Enabled,
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.027|                    SubscribedContent-353694Enabled,
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.028|                    SubscribedContent-353696Enabled,
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.029|                    SystemPaneSuggestionsEnabled,
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.030|                    SubscribedContent-338389Enabled,
::X|EN|db.cdm.suggestions.off.031|                    SilentInstalledAppsEnabled, PreInstalledAppsEnabled,
