::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.001|DESACTIVER WINDOWS SPOTLIGHT
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.002|
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.003|  Ce que c est    : Spotlight, ce sont les images tournantes de l'ecran de
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.004|                    verrouillage et du bureau, livrees avec des surcouches
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.005|                    de conseils et des liens promotionnels. Cette unique
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.006|                    valeur de strategie coupe toute la famille, pour tous
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.007|                    les comptes.
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.008|
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.009|  Effet reel      : Ecrit DisableWindowsSpotlightFeatures=1 sous HKLM.
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.010|
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.011|  Gain            : Plus de surcouches de conseils ni de liens
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.012|                    promotionnels sur votre ecran de verrouillage, et un
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.013|                    composant de moins qui telecharge du contenu. Mesurons
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.014|                    honnetement : aucun gain CPU ni memoire, et l'economie
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.015|                    reseau se limite a quelques images sur une rotation
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.016|                    lente. Reelle, mais assez faible pour ne pas etre la
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.017|                    raison de le faire.
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.018|
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.019|  Cout            : Vous perdez les photos tournantes, et si vous n'avez
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.020|                    jamais choisi votre propre image de verrouillage, vous
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.021|                    heritez d'un ecran uni. Il y a aussi un cout que les
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.022|                    autres reglages de confidentialite n'ont pas : voir la
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.023|                    rubrique problemes.
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.024|
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.025|  Defaut Windows  : Absente, Spotlight actif.
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.026|
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.027|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.028|    1                    : Toute la famille Spotlight est coupee : plus de
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.029|                           photos tournantes au verrouillage, plus de
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.030|                           theme Spotlight du bureau, plus de surcouches
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.031|                           de conseils ni de liens promotionnels. L'option
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.032|                           Windows Spotlight est retiree de la liste
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.033|                           deroulante de Personnalisation au lieu d'y
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.034|                           rester simplement non selectionnee, et comme la
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.035|                           valeur se trouve sous HKLM, elle s'applique a
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.036|                           tous les comptes de la machine.
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.037|    0                    : Explicitement autorise par strategie. Troisieme
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.038|                           etat : toujours signale comme gere, simplement
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.039|                           dans le sens permissif. Pour annuler, supprimez
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.040|                           au lieu d'ecrire 0.
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.041|    DELETE               : Absente, l'etat d'origine. Spotlight disponible
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.042|                           et choisi par chaque utilisateur dans
::T|FR|db.spotlight.off.043|                           Personnalisation.
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Gaming, serveur et portable ecrivent 1 : une
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.002|                         machine dont vous ne regardez guere l'ecran de
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.003|                         verrouillage n'a rien a y perdre, et sur un
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.004|                         portable ou une connexion limitee, ce
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.005|                         telechargement vaut la peine d'etre evite meme
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.006|                         s'il est modeste. La bureautique supprime, comme
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.007|                         Windows, pour deux raisons : un foyer apprecie
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.008|                         les photos du jour, et il s'agit d'une strategie
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.009|                         HKLM a l'echelle de la machine, qui marque
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.010|                         Personnalisation comme geree par votre
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.011|                         organisation pour toute personne qui ouvre une
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.012|                         session - exactement la banniere que ce script se
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.013|                         refuse a provoquer ailleurs. Si cette banniere
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.014|                         vous derange plus que les conseils, repondez 3 ou
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.015|                         5 meme sur une machine que vous depouilleriez par
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.016|                         ailleurs. Et si vous avez deja bloque les
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.017|                         applications sponsorisees, verifiez si l'ecran de
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.018|                         verrouillage n'est pas deja devenu uni : les deux
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.019|                         se recoupent.
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.020|
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.021|  Problemes connus : Avec la strategie a 1, Windows Spotlight disparait de
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.022|                     Personnalisation > Ecran de verrouillage et
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.023|                     Parametres affiche sur cette page une mention "gere
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.024|                     par votre organisation" pour tous les utilisateurs de
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.025|                     la machine, pas seulement celui qui a lance le
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.026|                     script.
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.027|
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.028|  Non verifie (en)  : I did not measure Spotlight's actual download volume
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.029|                      - it is a handful of images on a slow rotation, so
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.030|                      the bandwidth argument is small and should not be
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.031|                      sold as a headline. Whether
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.032|                      DisableWindowsConsumerFeatures=1 already suppresses
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.033|                      Spotlight on 25H2, which would make this value
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.034|                      redundant on any machine that answered yes there, is
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.035|                      unverified.
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.036|
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.037|  Cible           : reg add "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\Clou
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.038|                    dContent" /v "DisableWindowsSpotlightFeatures" /t
::X|FR|db.spotlight.off.039|                    REG_DWORD /d 1 /f (OPTY.bat line 1738)
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.001|DISABLE WINDOWS SPOTLIGHT
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.002|
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.003|  What it is      : Spotlight is the rotating lock-screen and desktop
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.004|                    imagery, delivered with tip overlays and promotional
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.005|                    links. This one policy value switches the whole family
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.006|                    off for every account.
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.007|
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.008|  Actual effect   : Writes DisableWindowsSpotlightFeatures=1 under HKLM.
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.009|
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.010|  Gain            : No tip overlays and no promotional links on your lock
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.011|                    screen, and one component that stops fetching content.
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.012|                    Size it honestly: there is no CPU or memory gain, and
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.013|                    the network saving is a few images on a slow rotation
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.014|                    - real, but small enough that it should not be the
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.015|                    reason you do this.
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.016|
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.017|  Cost            : You lose the rotating photographs, and if you never
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.018|                    chose your own lock-screen image you get a plain one.
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.019|                    There is also a cost the other privacy knobs do not
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.020|                    have - see bugs.
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.021|
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.022|  Windows default : Absent, Spotlight on.
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.023|
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.024|  Possible values:
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.025|    1                    : The entire Spotlight family is off: no rotating
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.026|                           lock-screen photographs, no Spotlight desktop
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.027|                           theme, no tip overlays, no promotional links.
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.028|                           The Windows Spotlight option is removed from
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.029|                           the Personalization dropdown rather than merely
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.030|                           unselected, and because the value lives in HKLM
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.031|                           it applies to every account on the machine.
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.032|    0                    : Explicitly allowed by policy. A third state -
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.033|                           still flagged as managed, just permissive.
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.034|                           Delete rather than write 0 to undo.
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.035|    DELETE               : Absent, the shipped state. Spotlight available
::T|EN|db.spotlight.off.036|                           and chosen per user in Personalization.
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.001|  Why these profiles : Gaming, server and laptop write 1: a machine whose
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.002|                       lock screen you barely look at has nothing to lose,
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.003|                       and on a laptop or a metered link the fetch is
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.004|                       worth avoiding even though it is small. Office
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.005|                       deletes, matching Windows, for two reasons - a
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.006|                       household enjoys the daily photographs, and this is
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.007|                       a machine-wide HKLM policy that stamps
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.008|                       Personalization as managed by your organization for
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.009|                       everyone who signs in, which is the exact banner
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.010|                       this script refuses to cause elsewhere. If that
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.011|                       banner bothers you more than the tips do, answer 3
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.012|                       or 5 even on a machine you would otherwise strip.
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.013|                       And if you already blocked sponsored apps, check
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.014|                       whether the lock screen has gone plain already; the
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.015|                       two overlap.
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.016|
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.017|  Known problems  : With the policy at 1, Windows Spotlight disappears
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.018|                    from Personalization > Lock screen and Settings shows
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.019|                    a managed-by-your-organization note on that page for
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.020|                    every user of the machine, not just the one who ran
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.021|                    the script.
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.022|
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.023|  Unverified      : I did not measure Spotlight's actual download volume -
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.024|                    it is a handful of images on a slow rotation, so the
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.025|                    bandwidth argument is small and should not be sold as
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.026|                    a headline. Whether DisableWindowsConsumerFeatures=1
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.027|                    already suppresses Spotlight on 25H2, which would make
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.028|                    this value redundant on any machine that answered yes
::X|EN|db.spotlight.off.029|                    there, is unverified.
