:: ---- rad.overlay.killkey (cleanup) -------------------------------
::P|rad.overlay.killkey|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.001|EFFACER LES RESIDUS OVERLAY ET INDEPENDENT FLIP
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.002|
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.003|  Ce que c est    : Quatre valeurs laissees par d'anciens scripts de
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.004|                    reglage, qui toutes suppriment une partie du chemin de
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.005|                    presentation moderne : OverlayTestMode, OverlayMinFPS
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.006|                    et DisableIndependentFlip sous Dwm, et DisableOverlays
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.007|                    sous GraphicsDrivers.
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.008|
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.009|  Effet reel      : Supprime celles des quatre qui existent, et le dit
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.010|                    valeur par valeur. Ecrire 0 ne retablirait pas le
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.011|                    defaut : seule l'absence le fait.
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.012|
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.013|  Gain            : Le GPU peut de nouveau utiliser les plans materiels et
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.014|                    l'independent flip : DWM saute une passe de
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.015|                    composition plein ecran par image tant qu'une fenetre
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.016|                    est au premier plan, et une fenetre borderless qui
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.017|                    couvre l'ecran peut basculer directement vers
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.018|                    l'affichage au lieu d'etre recopiee. Moins de
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.019|                    consommation GPU et un etage de latence en moins en
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.020|                    fenetre et en borderless. Rien ne change en plein
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.021|                    ecran exclusif.
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.022|
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.023|  Cout            : Si l'une d'elles masquait un vrai scintillement multi-
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.024|                    ecran, il peut revenir. Redemarrage necessaire pour
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.025|                    que ce soit effectif.
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.026|
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.027|  Defaut Windows  : Les quatre absentes.
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.028|
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.029|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.030|    DELETE               : Les quatre supprimees. :killkey interroge
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.031|                           d'abord et ne supprime que ce qui existe
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.032|                           reellement : il annonce « residu trouve »
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.033|                           plutot que de faire croire a une reparation sur
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.034|                           une machine propre. C'est l'etat d'origine pour
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.035|                           chacune des quatre.
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.036|    DisableIndependentFlip=1 :
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.037|        La seule valeur de cette liste qui ne fait pas partie de la
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.038|        recette MPO. L'independent flip, c'est ce qui permet a une fenetre
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.039|        borderless plein ecran, dont le swapchain couvre tout l'ecran, de
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.040|        voir ses tampons bascules directement vers l'affichage, sans la
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.041|        copie de DWM : c'est pour cela que le borderless peut se comporter
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.042|        comme du plein ecran exclusif en latence et en VRR. Forcer 1 remet
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.043|        la copie dans le chemin.
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.044|    OverlayTestMode=5    : L'interrupteur d'arret publie du MPO. DWM cesse
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.045|                           de proposer des plans materiels au pilote et
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.046|                           chaque image en fenetre repasse par une
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.047|                           composition complete du bureau.
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.048|    OverlayMinFPS=0 / DisableOverlays=1 :
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.049|        Les deux compagnons issus du folklore des scripts. Ni l'un ni
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.050|        l'autre ne figure dans la procedure publiee par Microsoft, et je
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.051|        n'ai trouve aucune documentation sur leur effet. On les supprime
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.052|        parce que l'absence est l'etat d'origine, pas parce qu'on
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.053|        comprendrait ce qu'elles font.
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.054|    0 on any of the four : Jamais un retour a l'origine. Pour les quatre,
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.055|                           le defaut Windows est l'inexistence de la
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.056|                           valeur : ecrire 0 laisse derriere un forcage
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.057|                           ecrit qui vaut zero. Seule la suppression
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.058|                           ramene la machine a l'etat d'usine - c'est
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.059|                           toute la raison d'etre de :killkey comme
::T|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.060|                           fonction distincte de :regset.
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Les cinq suppriment. Il n'y a pas de facon
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.002|                         honnete de decouper cela par intention : Windows
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.003|                         n'ecrit jamais aucune des quatre, donc sur chaque
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.004|                         profil le bon etat est le meme, et une difference
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.005|                         inventee ici serait une difference inventee a
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.006|                         partir de rien. Le profil serveur supprime aussi
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.007|                         : une machine sans ecran n'y gagne rien, mais
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.008|                         elle n'y perd rien non plus, et un residu qui ne
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.009|                         se manifeste qu'une fois un ecran branche est
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.010|                         justement celui qu'on retire pendant qu'on est
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.011|                         deja dans le registre. La seule machine qui
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.012|                         devrait garder OverlayTestMode est celle qui a un
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.013|                         scintillement reel et reproductible, et cette
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.014|                         decision releve de la carte de contournement.
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.015|
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.016|  Problemes connus : Aucun du fait de la suppression. Symptome concret si
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.017|                     l'on laisse DisableIndependentFlip=1 en place : les
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.018|                     jeux en fenetre sans bordure restent bloques a la
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.019|                     frequence du bureau, VRR inactif, et le conseil
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.020|                     habituel - passer en plein ecran exclusif - masque le
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.021|                     probleme au lieu de le corriger.
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.022|
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.023|  Non verifie (en)  : OPTY deliberately does NOT remove
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.024|                      UnsupportedMonitorModesAllowed from the same key,
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.025|                      and the in-file comment explains why: it is
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.026|                      dxgkrnl's custom-timing gate used by CRU and
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.027|                      Adrenalin custom modes, unrelated to MPO, and
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.028|                      nothing in the script would write it back. That
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.029|                      reasoning looks right to me, but it means this card
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.030|                      is not 'clear the whole key' and should not be
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.031|                      described as such.
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.032|
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.033|  Cible           : call :killkey on HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\Dwm
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.034|                    for OverlayTestMode, OverlayMinFPS,
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.035|                    DisableIndependentFlip, and on
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.036|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\GraphicsDrivers
::X|FR|rad.overlay.killkey.037|                    for DisableOverlays - OPTY.bat lines 1800-1803
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.001|CLEAR OVERLAY AND INDEPENDENT-FLIP LEFTOVERS
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.002|
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.003|  What it is      : Four values left behind by older tuning scripts, all
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.004|                    of which suppress part of the modern presentation
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.005|                    path: OverlayTestMode, OverlayMinFPS and
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.006|                    DisableIndependentFlip under Dwm, and DisableOverlays
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.007|                    under GraphicsDrivers.
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.008|
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.009|  Actual effect   : Deletes whichever of the four exist, and says so per
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.010|                    value. Writing 0 would not restore the default - only
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.011|                    absence does.
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.012|
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.013|  Gain            : The GPU can use hardware planes and independent flip
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.014|                    again: DWM skips a full-screen composite pass per
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.015|                    frame while a window is on top, and a covering
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.016|                    borderless window can flip straight to the display
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.017|                    instead of being copied. Lower GPU power and one less
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.018|                    stage of latency in windowed and borderless. Nothing
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.019|                    changes in exclusive fullscreen.
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.020|
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.021|  Cost            : If one of these was suppressing a real multi-monitor
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.022|                    flicker, it can come back. Reboot to take effect.
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.023|
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.024|  Windows default : All four absent.
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.025|
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.026|  Possible values:
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.027|    DELETE               : All four removed. :killkey queries first and
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.028|                           only deletes what is actually present, so it
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.029|                           reports 'leftover found' rather than pretending
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.030|                           it repaired something on a clean machine. This
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.031|                           is the shipped state for every one of the four.
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.032|    DisableIndependentFlip=1 :
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.033|        The one value on this list that is not part of the MPO recipe.
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.034|        Independent flip is what lets a fullscreen-borderless window whose
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.035|        swapchain covers the screen have its buffers flipped straight to
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.036|        the display, bypassing DWM's copy - it is why borderless can
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.037|        behave like exclusive fullscreen for latency and VRR. Forcing 1
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.038|        puts the copy back in.
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.039|    OverlayTestMode=5    : The published MPO kill switch. DWM stops
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.040|                           offering hardware planes to the driver and
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.041|                           every windowed frame goes through a full
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.042|                           desktop composite.
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.043|    OverlayMinFPS=0 / DisableOverlays=1 :
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.044|        The two script-folklore companions. Neither is in Microsoft's
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.045|        published procedure and I could not find documentation of their
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.046|        effect. They are deleted because absent is the shipped state, not
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.047|        because their effect is understood.
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.048|    0 on any of the four : Never a restore. For all four, the Windows
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.049|                           default is the value not existing, so writing 0
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.050|                           leaves a written override behind that happens
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.051|                           to read as zero. Only deletion returns the
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.052|                           machine to stock - which is the entire reason
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.053|                           :killkey exists as a separate helper from
::T|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.054|                           :regset.
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.001|  Why these profiles : All five delete. There is no honest way to split
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.002|                       this by intent: Windows never writes any of the
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.003|                       four, so on every profile the correct state is the
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.004|                       same one, and a difference invented here would be a
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.005|                       difference invented from nothing. The server
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.006|                       profile deletes too - a headless box gains nothing
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.007|                       from it, but it loses nothing either, and residue
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.008|                       that only matters once someone attaches a display
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.009|                       is exactly the residue worth removing while you are
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.010|                       already in the registry. The one machine that
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.011|                       should keep OverlayTestMode is one with a live,
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.012|                       reproducible flicker, and that decision belongs on
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.013|                       the flicker-workaround card.
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.014|
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.015|  Known problems  : None from removing them. Concrete symptom of leaving
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.016|                    DisableIndependentFlip=1 in place: borderless windowed
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.017|                    games stay stuck at the desktop refresh rate with VRR
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.018|                    inactive, and the usual advice - switch to exclusive
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.019|                    fullscreen - masks it instead of fixing it.
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.020|
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.021|  Unverified      : OPTY deliberately does NOT remove
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.022|                    UnsupportedMonitorModesAllowed from the same key, and
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.023|                    the in-file comment explains why: it is dxgkrnl's
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.024|                    custom-timing gate used by CRU and Adrenalin custom
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.025|                    modes, unrelated to MPO, and nothing in the script
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.026|                    would write it back. That reasoning looks right to me,
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.027|                    but it means this card is not 'clear the whole key'
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.028|                    and should not be described as such.
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.029|
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.030|  Target          : call :killkey on HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\Dwm
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.031|                    for OverlayTestMode, OverlayMinFPS,
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.032|                    DisableIndependentFlip, and on
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.033|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\GraphicsDrivers
::X|EN|rad.overlay.killkey.034|                    for DisableOverlays - OPTY.bat lines 1800-1803
