:: ---- rad.bcd.residue (risky) -----------------------------------
::P|rad.bcd.residue|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.001|RETIRER LES RESIDUS DE CONFIGURATION DE DEMARRAGE
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.002|
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.003|  Ce que c est    : Dix elements de configuration de demarrage poses sur
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.004|                    l'entree courante et qu'aucune installation de Windows
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.005|                    n'ecrit jamais : useplatformclock, useplatformtick,
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.006|                    disabledynamictick, tscsyncpolicy, numproc, onecpu,
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.007|                    maxproc, groupsize, truncatememory et removememory.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.008|                    Ils viennent des guides d'optimisation, de la fenetre
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.009|                    msconfig > Demarrer > Options avancees, ou d'une
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.010|                    session de diagnostic materiel que personne n'a
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.011|                    defaite.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.012|
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.013|  Effet reel      : Pour chaque element reellement present, lance bcdedit
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.014|                    /deletevalue {current} <element>. Si le volume systeme
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.015|                    est protege par BitLocker - detecte via HKLM\SYSTEM\Cu
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.016|                    rrentControlSet\Control\BitLockerStatus\BootStatus, le
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.017|                    seul signal insensible a la langue ici - il affiche
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.018|                    l'element et la commande exacte, et ne change rien.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.019|                    Redemarrage requis. usefirmwarepcisettings et
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.020|                    increaseuserva sont volontairement laisses tranquilles
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.021|                    : le premier peut deplacer l'attribution des
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.022|                    ressources PCI, le second est un element 32 bits
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.023|                    legitime, pas un residu.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.024|
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.025|  Gain            : Deux des dix font des degats reels et justifient le
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.026|                    redemarrage a eux seuls. useplatformclock impose le
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.027|                    HPET comme compteur de performance systeme : chaque
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.028|                    appel de temps devient une lecture sur le bus au lieu
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.029|                    d'une lecture de registre, et la latence DPC mesuree
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.030|                    comme la regularite d'affichage empirent au lieu de
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.031|                    s'ameliorer - on le vend comme un remede a la latence,
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.032|                    c'est un cout de latence. numproc, onecpu et groupsize
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.033|                    laissent le noyau tourner sur moins de processeurs
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.034|                    logiques que le CPU n'en a : le classique residu
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.035|                    msconfig ou un CPU a seize threads demarre sur quatre.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.036|                    truncatememory et removememory font disparaitre de la
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.037|                    RAM installee en « reserve materielle ». Si aucun des
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.038|                    dix n'est present - le cas courant sur une machine
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.039|                    jamais bidouillee - cette carte ne fait rien du tout,
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.040|                    et c'est un tres bon resultat.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.041|
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.042|  Cout            : Un redemarrage, et seulement pour les elements qui
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.043|                    etaient reellement la. Si vous en aviez pose un exprès
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.044|                    - onecpu ou numproc pour deboguer un pilote,
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.045|                    truncatememory pour reproduire une machine a faible
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.046|                    memoire - il disparait et il faudra le remettre.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.047|                    Aucune configuration Windows normale n'a besoin d'un
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.048|                    seul de ces dix elements.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.049|
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.050|  Defaut Windows  : Les dix absents de {current}. Le programme
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.051|                    d'installation de Windows n'en ecrit aucun, sur aucune
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.052|                    edition.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.053|
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.054|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.055|    DELETE               : Retirer de l'entree de demarrage {current}
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.056|                           chacun des dix elements presents, puis
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.057|                           redemarrer. C'est ce que font les cinq profils.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.058|                           Les elements absents sont ignores en silence :
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.059|                           sur une machine jamais bidouillee, cette carte
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.060|                           ne fait strictement rien.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.061|    SKIP                 : Signaler seulement, ne rien changer. C'est ce
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.062|                           que le script impose de lui-meme quand
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.063|                           BitLocker protege le volume systeme : il
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.064|                           affiche chaque element trouve et la commande
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.065|                           bcdedit exacte a lancer apres avoir suspendu
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.066|                           BitLocker.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.067|    useplatformclock yes : Impose le HPET comme source du compteur de
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.068|                           performance systeme a la place du TSC
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.069|                           invariant. Chaque appel a
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.070|                           QueryPerformanceCounter devient une lecture
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.071|                           MMIO sur le bus - des centaines de nanosecondes
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.072|                           - au lieu d'un RDTSC qui en coute quelques-
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.073|                           unes. Le code sensible au temps, ce qui inclut
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.074|                           tous les moteurs de jeu et toutes les piles
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.075|                           audio, paie ca a chaque appel, et la latence
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.076|                           DPC mesuree monte au lieu de descendre. Il n'y
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.077|                           a pas de bonne valeur : cet element ne devrait
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.078|                           pas exister.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.079|    useplatformtick yes  : Meme famille : force le timer de plateforme a
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.080|                           generer le tick periodique a la place du timer
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.081|                           APIC local de chaque coeur. Chaque tick devient
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.082|                           une transaction sur le bus, et les ticks ne
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.083|                           sont plus locaux au coeur. Meme verdict, on
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.084|                           l'enleve.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.085|    disabledynamictick yes :
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.086|        Desactive le noyau sans tick : l'interruption d'horloge continue
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.087|        de tomber a cadence fixe meme quand la machine n'a rien a faire,
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.088|        ce qui empeche les etats de repos profonds des coeurs et du
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.089|        package. Resultat : un repos plus chaud, plus bruyant, plus
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.090|        gourmand. Sur un portable, c'est de la batterie que vous brulez,
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.091|        tout simplement. La regularite de timing censee compenser n'est
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.092|        jamais apparue dans une mesure serieuse.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.093|    tscsyncpolicy Default / Legacy / Enhanced :
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.094|        Indique au noyau comment synchroniser le TSC entre les coeurs au
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.095|        demarrage. Forcer une politique releve du folklore des guides ;
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.096|        sur une machine multi-socket ou un CPU hybride coeurs P/coeurs E,
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.097|        la mauvaise politique est un bon moyen d'obtenir des bizarreries
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.098|        de source de temps que vous ne diagnostiquerez jamais. Absent, le
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.099|        noyau choisit d'apres ce que le CPU declare.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.100|    numproc N            : Limite a N le nombre de processeurs logiques
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.101|                           que le noyau demarre. C'est ce qu'ecrit la case
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.102|                           Nombre de processeurs dans msconfig, Demarrer >
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.103|                           Options avancees, et les gens l'oublient en
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.104|                           permanence. Symptome : le Gestionnaire des
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.105|                           taches affiche moins de processeurs logiques
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.106|                           que le CPU n'en a, et tout est plus lent sans
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.107|                           qu'aucun ecran ne l'explique.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.108|    onecpu yes           : Demarre sur un seul processeur logique. Un
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.109|                           element de debogage noyau, catastrophique quand
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.110|                           il traine.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.111|    maxproc yes          : Fait construire au noyau ses structures pour le
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.112|                           nombre maximal de processeurs que la plateforme
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.113|                           pourrait accueillir, en vue d'un ajout a chaud.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.114|                           Ne limite rien et reste globalement inoffensif
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.115|                           : un peu de pool non pagine gaspille. Il est
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.116|                           dans la liste parce que c'est un residu, pas
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.117|                           parce qu'il fait mal.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.118|    groupsize N          : Force la taille des groupes de processeurs (une
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.119|                           puissance de deux, jusqu'a 64). Regle a 2 ou 4,
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.120|                           la machine est decoupee en une multitude de
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.121|                           petits groupes, et comme une application
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.122|                           normale s'execute dans un seul groupe, elle ne
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.123|                           voit plus que deux ou quatre processeurs
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.124|                           logiques. Meme symptome visible que numproc,
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.125|                           mais bien plus difficile a reperer.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.126|    truncatememory <address in bytes> :
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.127|        Demande au systeme d'ignorer toute la memoire physique au-dessus
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.128|        de cette adresse. C'est la case Memoire maximale de msconfig.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.129|        Symptome : la page Systeme affiche « 32,0 Go installes (16,0 Go
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.130|        utilisable) » et les gens vont racheter de la RAM.
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.131|    removememory <bytes> : Retire ce nombre d'octets du haut de la memoire
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.132|                           utilisable. Meme famille, meme symptome, meme
::T|FR|rad.bcd.residue.133|                           reponse : ca n'a rien a faire la.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Les cinq suppriment, profil 5 compris, parce que
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.002|                         l'absence est l'etat livre pour chacun d'eux.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.003|                         C'est le cas le plus net de tout le lot ou la
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.004|                         bonne reponse ne depend pas de l'usage de la
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.005|                         machine : une entree de demarrage qui demarre sur
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.006|                         quatre de vos seize threads est aussi fausse pour
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.007|                         une machine de jeu que pour un serveur ou un
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.008|                         portable, et aucun usage ne gagne a forcer le
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.009|                         HPET comme horloge systeme. Le portable a une
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.010|                         raison de plus : disabledynamictick maintient
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.011|                         l'interruption d'horloge a cadence fixe pendant
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.012|                         les periodes d'inactivite, ce qui bloque les
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.013|                         etats de repos profonds du package et consomme de
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.014|                         la batterie en echange d'un benefice de timing
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.015|                         que personne n'a jamais mesure dans un jeu.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.016|
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.017|  Problemes connus : Symptomes concrets provoques par ces elements - pas
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.018|                     par leur suppression, qui n'a aucune casse connue. Le
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.019|                     Gestionnaire des taches qui affiche moins de
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.020|                     processeurs logiques que le CPU n'en a (numproc,
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.021|                     onecpu, groupsize). La page Systeme qui annonce «
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.022|                     32,0 Go installes (16,0 Go utilisable) »
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.023|                     (truncatememory, removememory). LatencyMon qui
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.024|                     rapporte des temps ISR/DPC eleves sans pilote
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.025|                     clairement fautif (useplatformclock,
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.026|                     useplatformtick). Un portable qui chauffe au repos et
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.027|                     se vide la nuit sans rien lancer
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.028|                     (disabledynamictick). Le seul risque operationnel est
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.029|                     BitLocker : modifier la configuration de demarrage
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.030|                     sur un volume protege expose a une demande de cle de
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.031|                     recuperation au prochain demarrage, d'ou le refus
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.032|                     d'ecrire dans ce cas.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.033|
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.034|  Non verifie (en)  : The BitLocker guard is deliberately conservative
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.035|                      rather than precise. BitLocker's default TPM-only
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.036|                      protector seals against a documented set of measured
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.037|                      boot settings; I cannot confirm that these ten
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.038|                      specific elements are inside that set, so I cannot
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.039|                      promise deleting one triggers a recovery prompt, nor
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.040|                      that it does not. Reporting instead of writing
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.041|                      whenever BitLocker is on is the right call under
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.042|                      that uncertainty. Suspending BitLocker for one
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.043|                      reboot is the safe way to apply them.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.044|
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.045|  Cible           : bcdedit /deletevalue "{current}" <element> for each
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.046|                    of: useplatformclock useplatformtick
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.047|                    disabledynamictick tscsyncpolicy numproc onecpu
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.048|                    maxproc groupsize truncatememory removememory. Loop at
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.049|                    OPTY.bat line 1986, helper :bcdresidue at lines
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.050|                    1994-2011. Presence is tested with bcdedit /enum
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.051|                    "{current}" / findstr /i /b. BitLocker guard reads
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.052|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\BitLockerStatus
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.053|                    /v BootStatus (line 1980); non-zero means report only.
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.054|                    Explicitly NOT touched: usefirmwarepcisettings and
::X|FR|rad.bcd.residue.055|                    increaseuserva.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.001|REMOVE BOOT CONFIGURATION LEFTOVERS
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.002|
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.003|  What it is      : Ten boot-configuration elements on the current boot
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.004|                    entry that no Windows installer ever writes:
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.005|                    useplatformclock, useplatformtick, disabledynamictick,
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.006|                    tscsyncpolicy, numproc, onecpu, maxproc, groupsize,
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.007|                    truncatememory and removememory. They come from tuning
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.008|                    guides, from msconfig's Boot > Advanced options
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.009|                    dialog, or from a hardware-debugging session somebody
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.010|                    never undid.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.011|
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.012|  Actual effect   : For each element that is actually present, runs
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.013|                    bcdedit /deletevalue {current} <element>. If the OS
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.014|                    volume is BitLocker-protected - read from HKLM\SYSTEM\
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.015|                    CurrentControlSet\Control\BitLockerStatus\BootStatus,
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.016|                    which is the one locale-proof signal here - it prints
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.017|                    the element and the exact command instead and changes
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.018|                    nothing. Reboot required. usefirmwarepcisettings and
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.019|                    increaseuserva are deliberately left alone: the first
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.020|                    can move PCI resource assignment, the second is a
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.021|                    legitimate 32-bit element and not wreckage.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.022|
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.023|  Gain            : Two of the ten do real damage and justify the reboot
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.024|                    by themselves. useplatformclock forces the HPET as the
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.025|                    system performance counter, so every timing call
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.026|                    becomes a bus read instead of a register read and
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.027|                    measured DPC latency and frame pacing get worse rather
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.028|                    than better - it is sold as a latency fix and it is a
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.029|                    latency cost. numproc, onecpu and groupsize leave the
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.030|                    kernel running on fewer logical processors than the
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.031|                    CPU has, the classic msconfig leftover where a
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.032|                    sixteen-thread CPU boots on four. truncatememory and
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.033|                    removememory make installed RAM vanish into hardware-
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.034|                    reserved. If none of the ten are present - the common
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.035|                    case on a machine that was never tweaked - this card
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.036|                    does nothing at all, and that is a perfectly good
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.037|                    outcome.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.038|
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.039|  Cost            : A reboot, and only for the elements that were actually
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.040|                    there. If you set one deliberately - onecpu or numproc
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.041|                    for driver debugging, truncatememory to reproduce a
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.042|                    low-memory condition - you lose it and have to set it
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.043|                    again. Nothing in a normal Windows configuration
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.044|                    requires any of the ten.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.045|
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.046|  Windows default : All ten absent from {current}. Windows Setup writes
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.047|                    none of them, on any edition.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.048|
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.049|  Possible values:
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.050|    DELETE               : Remove every one of the ten that is present
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.051|                           from the {current} boot entry, then reboot.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.052|                           This is what all five profiles do. Elements
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.053|                           that are not present are skipped silently, so
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.054|                           on a machine that was never tweaked this whole
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.055|                           card is a no-op.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.056|    SKIP                 : Report only, change nothing. This is what the
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.057|                           script forces on its own when BitLocker
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.058|                           protects the OS volume: it prints each element
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.059|                           it found and the exact bcdedit command to run
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.060|                           after suspending BitLocker.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.061|    useplatformclock yes : Forces the HPET as the system performance
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.062|                           counter source instead of the invariant TSC.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.063|                           Every QueryPerformanceCounter call becomes an
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.064|                           MMIO read across the bus - hundreds of
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.065|                           nanoseconds - instead of an RDTSC costing a
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.066|                           few. Timing-heavy code, which includes every
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.067|                           game engine and every audio stack, pays that on
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.068|                           each call, and measured DPC latency goes up,
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.069|                           not down. There is no correct value: the
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.070|                           element should not exist.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.071|    useplatformtick yes  : Same family: forces the platform timer to
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.072|                           generate the periodic tick instead of the per-
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.073|                           core local APIC timer. Every tick becomes a bus
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.074|                           transaction, and the ticks are no longer core-
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.075|                           local. Same verdict, remove it.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.076|    disabledynamictick yes :
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.077|        Turns off the tickless kernel: the timer interrupt keeps firing at
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.078|        a fixed rate even when the machine has nothing to do, which
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.079|        prevents deep core and package idle states. That means a warmer,
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.080|        noisier, thirstier idle. On a laptop it is straightforwardly
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.081|        battery you are burning. The timing consistency it is supposed to
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.082|        buy has never shown up in a careful measurement.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.083|    tscsyncpolicy Default / Legacy / Enhanced :
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.084|        Tells the kernel how to synchronise the TSC across cores at boot.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.085|        Forcing a policy is guide folklore; on a multi-socket machine or a
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.086|        hybrid P-core/E-core CPU, the wrong policy is a way to get time-
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.087|        source oddities you will never diagnose. Absent lets the kernel
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.088|        pick from what the CPU reports.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.089|    numproc N            : Caps the number of logical processors the
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.090|                           kernel starts at N. This is what msconfig's
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.091|                           Boot > Advanced options > Number of processors
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.092|                           box writes, and people leave it behind
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.093|                           constantly. Symptom: Task Manager shows fewer
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.094|                           logical processors than the CPU has, and
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.095|                           everything is slower for a reason nothing on
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.096|                           screen explains.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.097|    onecpu yes           : Boots on a single logical processor. A kernel-
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.098|                           debugging element, catastrophic as a leftover.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.099|    maxproc yes          : Makes the kernel build its structures for the
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.100|                           maximum number of processors the platform could
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.101|                           ever have, for hot-add support. It does not cap
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.102|                           anything and is mostly harmless - a small
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.103|                           amount of wasted non-paged pool. It is on the
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.104|                           list because it is wreckage, not because it
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.105|                           hurts.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.106|    groupsize N          : Forces the size of processor groups (a power of
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.107|                           two, up to 64). Set to 2 or 4, the machine gets
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.108|                           carved into many tiny groups, and since a
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.109|                           normal application runs inside a single group
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.110|                           it now sees two or four logical processors.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.111|                           Same visible symptom as numproc, harder to
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.112|                           spot.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.113|    truncatememory <address in bytes> :
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.114|        Tells the OS to ignore all physical memory above that address.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.115|        This is msconfig's Maximum memory box. Symptom: System shows
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.116|        "Installed 32.0 GB (16.0 GB usable)" and people go buy RAM.
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.117|    removememory <bytes> : Removes that many bytes from the top of usable
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.118|                           memory. Same family, same symptom, same answer:
::T|EN|rad.bcd.residue.119|                           it should not be there.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.001|  Why these profiles : All five delete, profile 5 included, because absent
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.002|                       is the shipped state for every single one of these.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.003|                       This is the clearest case in the set where the
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.004|                       right answer does not depend on what the machine is
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.005|                       for: a boot entry that starts on four of your
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.006|                       sixteen threads is wrong for a gaming rig, a server
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.007|                       and a laptop equally, and there is no role that
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.008|                       benefits from the HPET being forced as the system
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.009|                       clock. The laptop has one extra reason on top:
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.010|                       disabledynamictick keeps the timer interrupt firing
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.011|                       at a fixed rate while the machine idles, which
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.012|                       blocks the deep package idle states and burns
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.013|                       battery for a timing benefit nobody has ever
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.014|                       measured in a game.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.015|
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.016|  Known problems  : Concrete symptoms these elements cause - not symptoms
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.017|                    of removing them, which has no known breakage. Task
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.018|                    Manager showing fewer logical processors than the CPU
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.019|                    has (numproc, onecpu, groupsize). System reporting
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.020|                    "Installed 32.0 GB (16.0 GB usable)" (truncatememory,
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.021|                    removememory). LatencyMon reporting high ISR/DPC times
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.022|                    with no driver obviously at fault (useplatformclock,
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.023|                    useplatformtick). A laptop that idles hot and drains
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.024|                    overnight with nothing running (disabledynamictick).
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.025|                    The one operational hazard is BitLocker: edit the boot
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.026|                    configuration on a protected volume and you risk a
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.027|                    recovery-key prompt at the next boot, which is why the
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.028|                    script refuses to write in that case.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.029|
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.030|  Unverified      : The BitLocker guard is deliberately conservative
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.031|                    rather than precise. BitLocker's default TPM-only
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.032|                    protector seals against a documented set of measured
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.033|                    boot settings; I cannot confirm that these ten
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.034|                    specific elements are inside that set, so I cannot
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.035|                    promise deleting one triggers a recovery prompt, nor
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.036|                    that it does not. Reporting instead of writing
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.037|                    whenever BitLocker is on is the right call under that
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.038|                    uncertainty. Suspending BitLocker for one reboot is
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.039|                    the safe way to apply them.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.040|
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.041|  Target          : bcdedit /deletevalue "{current}" <element> for each
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.042|                    of: useplatformclock useplatformtick
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.043|                    disabledynamictick tscsyncpolicy numproc onecpu
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.044|                    maxproc groupsize truncatememory removememory. Loop at
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.045|                    OPTY.bat line 1986, helper :bcdresidue at lines
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.046|                    1994-2011. Presence is tested with bcdedit /enum
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.047|                    "{current}" / findstr /i /b. BitLocker guard reads
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.048|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\BitLockerStatus
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.049|                    /v BootStatus (line 1980); non-zero means report only.
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.050|                    Explicitly NOT touched: usefirmwarepcisettings and
::X|EN|rad.bcd.residue.051|                    increaseuserva.
