::P|net.tcp.defaults.netdns|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.001|REAFFIRMER LES TROIS REGLAGES TCP GLOBAUX STANDARD
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.002|
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.003|  Ce que c est    : Trois reglages TCP valables pour toute la machine :
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.004|                    l'ajustement automatique de la fenetre de reception
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.005|                    (jusqu'ou Windows accepte de la faire grandir), les
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.006|                    heuristiques de mise a l'echelle de fenetre (qui
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.007|                    laissent Windows revenir sur cet ajustement chemin par
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.008|                    chemin), et le RSS au niveau TCP, qui repartit le
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.009|                    traitement en reception sur plusieurs coeurs.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.010|
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.011|  Effet reel      : OPTY ecrit autotuninglevel=normal, heuristics=disabled
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.012|                    et rss=enabled sans condition, sans lire d'abord les
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.013|                    valeurs en place. Effet immediat sur toute la machine,
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.014|                    sans redemarrage.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.015|
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.016|  Gain            : Sur une machine Windows 11 non trafiquee, aucun. Les
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.017|                    trois sont deja a ces valeurs - verifie en direct ici,
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.018|                    et les heuristiques de mise a l'echelle sont livrees
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.019|                    desactivees depuis Windows 8.1. L'etape ne sert pas a
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.020|                    ameliorer mais a reparer : les optimiseurs de jeu et
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.021|                    les tutos de forum ecrivent regulierement
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.022|                    autotuninglevel=disabled, ce qui bloque la fenetre de
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.023|                    reception a 64 Ko et effondre le debit sur tout chemin
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.024|                    long ou rapide. Ceci le remet en place.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.025|
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.026|  Cout            : Rien sur une machine d'origine. Si vous aviez
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.027|                    volontairement regle TCP pour un lien inhabituel -
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.028|                    satellite, WAN a forte latence, banc de test - votre
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.029|                    reglage est ecrase sans avertissement et sans trace de
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.030|                    ce qu'il valait.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.031|
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.032|  Defaut Windows  : autotuninglevel=normal, rss=enabled et les
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.033|                    heuristiques de mise a l'echelle desactivees sont
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.034|                    toutes des valeurs Windows d'origine. netsh int tcp
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.035|                    set heuristics default rend la main a Windows et
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.036|                    aboutit au meme comportement.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.037|
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.038|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.039|    autotuninglevel=normal :
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.040|        Windows dimensionne automatiquement la fenetre de reception TCP et
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.041|        la fait grandir jusqu'au produit debit x latence du chemin. Valeur
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.042|        d'origine.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.043|    autotuninglevel=disabled :
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.044|        La fenetre de reception est bloquee a 64 Ko et la mise a l'echelle
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.045|        n'est jamais negociee. Sur un chemin a 100 ms, un seul flux TCP
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.046|        plafonne vers 5 Mbit/s. C'est la valeur qu'ecrivent les guides
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.047|        d'optimisation.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.048|    autotuninglevel=highlyrestricted :
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.049|        La fenetre ne depasse que tres legerement les 64 Ko par defaut.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.050|    autotuninglevel=restricted :
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.051|        La fenetre grandit moderement au-dela du defaut, mais reste loin
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.052|        de ce qu'exige un chemin long et rapide.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.053|    autotuninglevel=experimental :
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.054|        La fenetre peut atteindre des valeurs extremes, jusqu'a un facteur
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.055|        d'echelle de 1 Go. Cela gaspille du pool non pagine et aucun usage
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.056|        domestique n'en a besoin.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.057|    heuristics=disabled  : Windows cesse d'appliquer ses heuristiques de
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.058|                           mise a l'echelle memorisees par chemin et
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.059|                           respecte le niveau d'autotuning que vous avez
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.060|                           fixe.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.061|    heuristics=enabled   : Windows peut reduire en silence le facteur
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.062|                           d'echelle sur les chemins qu'il juge
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.063|                           problematiques, passant outre votre niveau
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.064|                           d'autotuning sans rien dire.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.065|    heuristics=default   : Cesse d'imposer une valeur et rend la decision
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.066|                           a la politique interne de Windows, desactivee
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.067|                           depuis Windows 8.1 : le comportement observable
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.068|                           est donc le meme que heuristics=disabled.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.069|    rss=enabled          : Le traitement des paquets recus est reparti sur
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.070|                           plusieurs coeurs au niveau TCP. Valeur
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.071|                           d'origine.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.072|    rss=disabled         : Tout le traitement en reception tombe sur un
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.073|                           seul coeur, qui sature avant le lien sur une
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.074|                           connexion rapide.
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.075|    rss=default          : Cesse d'imposer une valeur et rend la decision
::T|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.076|                           a Windows, dont la politique est enabled.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq colonnes identiques, parce qu'il n'y a rien
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.002|                         a faire varier. Ces trois valeurs SONT les
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.003|                         valeurs d'usine : gaming, serveur, bureautique et
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.004|                         portable les veulent toutes, et la colonne
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.005|                         Windows aussi, puisque les ecrire est precisement
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.006|                         la maniere de ramener une machine trafiquee a
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.007|                         l'etat livre. Le seul refus legitime vient de
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.008|                         quelqu'un qui a choisi sciemment un autre niveau
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.009|                         d'autotuning pour un lien precis.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.010|
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.011|  Non verifie (en)  : That Window Scaling Heuristics ships disabled rests
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.012|                      on documented Windows 8.1-and-later behaviour plus
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.013|                      one live Windows 11 25H2 reading. Microsoft does not
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.014|                      restate it per release, so it is not sourced from a
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.015|                      25H2 document.
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.016|
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.017|  Cible           : netsh int tcp set global autotuninglevel=normal ;
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.018|                    netsh int tcp set heuristics disabled ; netsh int tcp
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.019|                    set global rss=enabled - the three lines at
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.020|                    :netdns_tcp (OPTY.bat ~590), run unconditionally
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.021|                    during the maintenance pass right after ipconfig
::X|FR|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.022|                    /flushdns
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.001|RE-ASSERT THE THREE STANDARD TCP GLOBALS
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.002|
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.003|  What it is      : Three machine-wide TCP/IP settings: receive-window
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.004|                    autotuning (how large a window Windows will
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.005|                    negotiate), Window Scaling Heuristics (whether Windows
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.006|                    second-guesses that autotuning per path), and Receive
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.007|                    Side Scaling at the TCP layer, which spreads receive
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.008|                    processing across CPU cores.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.009|
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.010|  Actual effect   : OPTY writes autotuninglevel=normal,
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.011|                    heuristics=disabled and rss=enabled unconditionally,
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.012|                    without reading the current values first. Machine-
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.013|                    wide, immediate, no reboot.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.014|
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.015|  Gain            : On an untouched Windows 11 machine, none. All three
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.016|                    are already at these values - verified live here, and
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.017|                    Window Scaling Heuristics has shipped disabled since
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.018|                    Windows 8.1. The step exists to undo damage, not to
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.019|                    improve anything: gaming optimizers and forum guides
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.020|                    routinely write autotuninglevel=disabled, which pins
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.021|                    the receive window at 64 KB and destroys throughput on
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.022|                    any long or fast path. This puts it back.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.023|
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.024|  Cost            : Nothing on a stock machine. If you had deliberately
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.025|                    tuned TCP for an unusual link - satellite, high-
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.026|                    latency WAN, a lab setup - your setting is overwritten
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.027|                    silently, with no record of what it was.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.028|
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.029|  Windows default : autotuninglevel=normal, rss=enabled and Window Scaling
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.030|                    Heuristics disabled are all Windows defaults. netsh
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.031|                    int tcp set heuristics default hands the decision back
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.032|                    to Windows and lands on the same behaviour.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.033|
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.034|  Possible values:
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.035|    autotuninglevel=normal :
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.036|        Windows sizes the TCP receive window automatically, scaling it up
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.037|        to the bandwidth-delay product of the path. Shipped value.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.038|    autotuninglevel=disabled :
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.039|        The receive window is pinned at 64 KB and window scaling is never
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.040|        negotiated. On a 100 ms path that caps a single TCP stream at
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.041|        roughly 5 Mbit/s. This is the value optimizer guides write.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.042|    autotuninglevel=highlyrestricted :
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.043|        The window may grow only slightly beyond the 64 KB default.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.044|    autotuninglevel=restricted :
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.045|        The window grows moderately beyond the default, still well below
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.046|        what a long fast path needs.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.047|    autotuninglevel=experimental :
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.048|        The window may grow to extreme values, up to a 1 GB scale factor.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.049|        It wastes non-paged pool and no home path needs it.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.050|    heuristics=disabled  : Windows stops applying its stored per-path
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.051|                           Window Scaling Heuristics and honours the
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.052|                           autotuning level you set.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.053|    heuristics=enabled   : Windows may silently reduce the window scale
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.054|                           factor on paths it judges problematic,
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.055|                           overriding your autotuning level without
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.056|                           telling you.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.057|    heuristics=default   : Stops asserting a value and hands the decision
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.058|                           to the Windows built-in policy, which has been
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.059|                           disabled since Windows 8.1 - so the observable
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.060|                           behaviour matches heuristics=disabled.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.061|    rss=enabled          : Received-packet processing is spread across
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.062|                           several CPU cores at the TCP layer. Shipped
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.063|                           value.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.064|    rss=disabled         : All receive processing lands on a single core,
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.065|                           which saturates before the link does on a fast
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.066|                           connection.
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.067|    rss=default          : Stops asserting a value and hands the decision
::T|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.068|                           to Windows, whose policy is enabled.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.001|  Why these profiles : Five identical columns, because there is nothing
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.002|                       here to vary. These three values ARE the shipped
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.003|                       defaults, so gaming, server, office and laptop all
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.004|                       want them, and the Windows column wants them too -
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.005|                       writing them is exactly how a mangled machine gets
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.006|                       back to shipped. The only owner who should decline
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.007|                       is one who knowingly set a non-default autotuning
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.008|                       level for a specific link.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.009|
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.010|  Unverified      : That Window Scaling Heuristics ships disabled rests on
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.011|                    documented Windows 8.1-and-later behaviour plus one
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.012|                    live Windows 11 25H2 reading. Microsoft does not
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.013|                    restate it per release, so it is not sourced from a
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.014|                    25H2 document.
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.015|
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.016|  Target          : netsh int tcp set global autotuninglevel=normal ;
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.017|                    netsh int tcp set heuristics disabled ; netsh int tcp
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.018|                    set global rss=enabled - the three lines at
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.019|                    :netdns_tcp (OPTY.bat ~590), run unconditionally
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.020|                    during the maintenance pass right after ipconfig
::X|EN|net.tcp.defaults.netdns.021|                    /flushdns
