:: ---- sfc.scannow (repair) ---------------------------------------
::P|sfc.scannow|RUN|RUN|RUN|RUN|SKIP|
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.001|SFC - VERIFICATION DES FICHIERS SYSTEME
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.002|
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.003|  Ce que c est    : Le Verificateur des fichiers systeme controle chaque
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.004|                    fichier systeme protege par rapport au magasin de
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.005|                    composants et restaure ceux qui ne correspondent pas.
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.006|
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.007|  Effet reel      : Il lit et empreinte les fichiers proteges, remplace
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.008|                    les corrompus par la copie issue de WinSxS, et
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.009|                    consigne tout dans CBS.log. Sur une machine saine, il
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.010|                    se termine par aucune violation d'integrite trouvee et
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.011|                    ne change strictement rien.
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.012|
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.013|  Gain            : Reel quand des fichiers sont vraiment corrompus :
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.014|                    l'Explorateur qui plante au lancement, une page des
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.015|                    Parametres qui refuse de s'ouvrir, une DLL systeme
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.016|                    absente ou erronee. Sur une machine sans symptome,
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.017|                    c'est une lecture de cinq a quinze minutes qui finit
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.018|                    par un rapport propre. Voila la valeur exacte de
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.019|                    l'operation : c'est un diagnostic, et un diagnostic
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.020|                    propre vaut quelque chose, mais ce n'est pas un gain
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.021|                    de vitesse.
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.022|
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.023|  Cout            : Cinq a quinze minutes de disque et de processeur
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.024|                    fortement sollicites. Si le magasin de composants est
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.025|                    lui-meme abime, SFC ne peut rien reparer : c'est
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.026|                    precisement pour cela que DISM passe en premier dans
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.027|                    l'ordre d'OPTY. Aucun risque pour vos donnees, a aucun
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.028|                    moment.
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.029|
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.030|  Defaut Windows  : Sans objet - Windows ne lance jamais SFC de lui-meme.
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.031|                    Aucune tache planifiee ne le fait.
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.032|
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.033|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.034|    RUN                  : sfc /scannow. Calcule l'empreinte de chaque
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.035|                           fichier systeme protege, la compare au
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.036|                           manifeste du magasin de composants, remplace
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.037|                           toute divergence par la copie issue de WinSxS,
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.038|                           et consigne son travail dans
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.039|                           %WinDir%\Logs\CBS\CBS.log. Il ne touche que les
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.040|                           binaires de Windows : jamais vos applications,
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.041|                           vos documents ni vos reglages.
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.042|    VERIFYONLY           : sfc /verifyonly. Meme analyse, meme duree, mais
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.043|                           il signale les divergences au lieu de les
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.044|                           reparer. Utile pour savoir avant que quoi que
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.045|                           ce soit ne soit remplace. OPTY ne propose pas
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.046|                           cette variante.
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.047|    SKIP                 : Rien ne s'execute. Aucun fichier n'est lu, rien
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.048|                           ne change. C'est ce que fait Windows tout seul
::T|FR|sfc.scannow.049|                           : aucune tache planifiee ne lance SFC.
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Quatre colonnes RUN identiques, parce que la
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.002|                         corruption de fichiers n'est pas un usage, c'est
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.003|                         un accident, et elle frappe un PC de jeu aussi
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.004|                         facilement qu'un poste bureautique. La colonne
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.005|                         portable reste a RUN, avec une reserve qui releve
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.006|                         du bon sens plutot que du profil : l'analyse
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.007|                         occupe un coeur et malmene le disque pendant un
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.008|                         quart d'heure, alors branchez-vous d'abord. La
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.009|                         colonne Windows est a SKIP parce que ne rien
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.010|                         faire est vraiment le comportement livre : rien
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.011|                         dans Windows ne planifie SFC, et pretendre le
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.012|                         contraire fausserait la notion de defaut.
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.013|
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.014|  Cible           : sfc /scannow - OPTY.bat line 661, inside the :sfc
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.015|                    label. Step id clean.sfc, declared _F in the step
::X|FR|sfc.scannow.016|                    table (auto-full only) at OPTY.bat line 19131.
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.001|SFC SYSTEM FILE CHECK
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.002|
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.003|  What it is      : System File Checker verifies every protected Windows
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.004|                    system file against the component store and restores
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.005|                    any that do not match.
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.006|
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.007|  Actual effect   : Reads and hashes protected files, replaces corrupt
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.008|                    ones from WinSxS, records everything in CBS.log. On a
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.009|                    healthy machine it finishes with found no integrity
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.010|                    violations and changes nothing at all.
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.011|
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.012|  Gain            : Real when files are genuinely corrupt - Explorer
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.013|                    crashing on launch, a Settings page that will not
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.014|                    open, a missing or wrong system DLL. On a machine with
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.015|                    no symptoms it is a five-to-fifteen minute read that
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.016|                    ends in a clean report. That is a fair description of
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.017|                    the value: it is a diagnosis, and a clean diagnosis is
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.018|                    worth something, but it is not a speed-up.
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.019|
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.020|  Cost            : Five to fifteen minutes of heavy disk and CPU. If the
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.021|                    component store itself is damaged, SFC cannot repair
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.022|                    anything, which is exactly why DISM runs first in
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.023|                    OPTY's order. No risk to your data at any point.
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.024|
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.025|  Windows default : Not applicable - Windows never runs SFC by itself.
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.026|                    There is no scheduled task for it.
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.027|
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.028|  Possible values:
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.029|    RUN                  : sfc /scannow. Hashes every protected system
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.030|                           file, compares each against the manifest in the
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.031|                           component store, replaces any mismatch with the
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.032|                           copy from WinSxS, and writes what it did to
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.033|                           %WinDir%\Logs\CBS\CBS.log. It touches Windows
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.034|                           binaries only - never your applications,
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.035|                           documents or settings.
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.036|    VERIFYONLY           : sfc /verifyonly. Same scan, same duration, but
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.037|                           it reports mismatches instead of repairing
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.038|                           them. Useful when you want to know before
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.039|                           anything is replaced. OPTY does not offer this
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.040|                           variant.
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.041|    SKIP                 : Nothing runs. No file is read, nothing changes.
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.042|                           This is what Windows does on its own - there is
::T|EN|sfc.scannow.043|                           no scheduled task that runs SFC.
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.001|  Why these profiles : Four identical RUN columns, because file corruption
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.002|                       is not a use case, it is an accident, and it
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.003|                       happens to a gaming desktop exactly as readily as
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.004|                       to an office PC. The laptop column stays RUN with
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.005|                       one caveat that belongs in your head rather than in
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.006|                       a profile: the scan pins a core and hammers the
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.007|                       disk for up to a quarter of an hour, so plug in
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.008|                       first. The Windows column is SKIP because absent is
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.009|                       genuinely the shipped behaviour - nothing in
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.010|                       Windows schedules SFC, and pretending otherwise
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.011|                       would misrepresent the default.
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.012|
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.013|  Target          : sfc /scannow - OPTY.bat line 661, inside the :sfc
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.014|                    label. Step id clean.sfc, declared _F in the step
::X|EN|sfc.scannow.015|                    table (auto-full only) at OPTY.bat line 19131.
