::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.001|8.3 SHORT NAMES BACK TO PER-VOLUME
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.002|
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.003|  What it is      : Whether NTFS also creates an old DOS-style 8.3 name
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.004|                    for each file. This is the restore-menu version: same
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.005|                    write, reached when you are undoing someone else's
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.006|                    tuning rather than setting up.
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.007|
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.008|  Actual effect   : Sets mode 2 - each volume decides, instead of a global
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.009|                    on or off. Applies to names created from now on only;
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.010|                    short names that already exist stay, and short names
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.011|                    that were never created during a period at value 1 do
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.012|                    not appear retroactively.
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.013|
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.014|  Gain            : No measurable speed gain, and this card does not
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.015|                    pretend otherwise. What it removes is a global
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.016|                    override that can break old installers and
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.017|                    uninstallers relying on short paths. That is the
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.018|                    entire benefit and it is a real one.
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.019|
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.020|  Cost            : Nothing. This is a pure repair back to the shipped
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.021|                    value.
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.022|
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.023|  Windows default : 2.
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.024|
::T|EN|gr.8dot3.default.025|  Possible values:
