:: ---- rp.point.create (preference) -----------------------------------
::P|rp.point.create|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|SKIP|
::T|FR|rp.point.create.001|POINT DE RESTAURATION AVANT MODIFICATION
::T|FR|rp.point.create.002|
::T|FR|rp.point.create.003|  Ce que c est    : Avant toute operation destructive, OPTY appelle
::T|FR|rp.point.create.004|                    :restore_point une fois par session. Il active la
::T|FR|rp.point.create.005|                    protection du systeme sur le disque systeme si elle
::T|FR|rp.point.create.006|                    etait coupee, met brievement
::T|FR|rp.point.create.007|                    SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency a 0 pour que
::T|FR|rp.point.create.008|                    Windows ne refuse pas un second point dans les 24
::T|FR|rp.point.create.009|                    heures, cree un point nomme d'apres la version d'OPTY,
::T|FR|rp.point.create.010|                    puis reecrit 1440.
::T|FR|rp.point.create.011|
::T|FR|rp.point.create.012|  Effet reel      : Un point de restauration fige les ruches de registre
::T|FR|rp.point.create.013|                    et les fichiers systeme proteges via VSS. Il ne fige
::T|FR|rp.point.create.014|                    pas vos documents : ce n'est donc pas une sauvegarde.
::T|FR|rp.point.create.015|                    Le verrou est remis a la valeur Windows juste apres,
::T|FR|rp.point.create.016|                    OPTY ne laisse donc pas la protection du systeme
::T|FR|rp.point.create.017|                    modifiee derriere lui.
::T|FR|rp.point.create.018|
::T|FR|rp.point.create.019|  Gain            : Si une ecriture registre du menu 2 se passe mal sur
::T|FR|rp.point.create.020|                    votre machine, vous pouvez revenir en arriere depuis
::T|FR|rp.point.create.021|                    la restauration du systeme ou depuis l'environnement
::T|FR|rp.point.create.022|                    de recuperation. C'est la seule annulation dont
::T|FR|rp.point.create.023|                    dispose le script.
::T|FR|rp.point.create.024|
::T|FR|rp.point.create.025|  Cout            : De l'espace de cliches instantanes sur C:, souvent
::T|FR|rp.point.create.026|                    quelques centaines de Mo a deux Go, Windows supprimant
::T|FR|rp.point.create.027|                    le point LE PLUS ANCIEN quand son quota est plein.
::T|FR|rp.point.create.028|                    Plus 10 a 60 secondes. Si la protection du systeme
::T|FR|rp.point.create.029|                    etait volontairement coupee, OPTY l'active et ne la
::T|FR|rp.point.create.030|                    recoupe jamais : cette partie-la est definitive.
::T|FR|rp.point.create.031|
::T|FR|rp.point.create.032|  Defaut Windows  : Sur une installation propre de Windows 11, la
::T|FR|rp.point.create.033|                    protection du systeme est DESACTIVEE pour le disque
::T|FR|rp.point.create.034|                    systeme, et Windows ne cree des points que selon son
::T|FR|rp.point.create.035|                    propre calendrier, jamais a la demande. Beaucoup
::T|FR|rp.point.create.036|                    d'images constructeur la livrent activee.
::T|FR|rp.point.create.037|
::T|FR|rp.point.create.038|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|rp.point.create.039|    APPLY                : La protection du systeme est activee sur le
::T|FR|rp.point.create.040|                           disque systeme si elle etait coupee, le verrou
::T|FR|rp.point.create.041|                           des 24 heures est leve le temps de l'appel, un
::T|FR|rp.point.create.042|                           point de restauration est ecrit, puis le verrou
::T|FR|rp.point.create.043|                           est remis a 1440 minutes. La protection reste
::T|FR|rp.point.create.044|                           active ensuite.
::T|FR|rp.point.create.045|    SKIP                 : Rien n'est active et aucun point n'est pris. La
::T|FR|rp.point.create.046|                           machine garde exactement l'etat de protection
::T|FR|rp.point.create.047|                           qu'elle avait, et les ecritures registre qui
::T|FR|rp.point.create.048|                           suivent n'ont pas d'annulation en un clic.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Quatre profils sont identiques parce qu'un filet
::X|FR|rp.point.create.002|                         de securite ne depend pas de l'usage de la
::X|FR|rp.point.create.003|                         machine. Seul le profil WINDOWS passe son tour,
::X|FR|rp.point.create.004|                         pour une raison mecanique : activer la protection
::X|FR|rp.point.create.005|                         du systeme est un changement de configuration
::X|FR|rp.point.create.006|                         permanent, et ce profil sert justement a ne pas
::X|FR|rp.point.create.007|                         toucher a l'etat d'origine. Si votre image a deja
::X|FR|rp.point.create.008|                         la protection activee, repondre oui ne coute
::X|FR|rp.point.create.009|                         qu'une minute et un peu d'espace de cliches.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.010|
::X|FR|rp.point.create.011|  Non verifie (en)  : Whether System Protection ships on or off differs
::X|FR|rp.point.create.012|                      between a clean Windows 11 install and OEM images.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.013|                      OPTY enables it and never turns it back off - only
::X|FR|rp.point.create.014|                      the creation-frequency throttle is restored.
::X|FR|rp.point.create.015|
::X|FR|rp.point.create.016|  Cible           : :restore_point, OPTY.bat 3990-4014 - powershell
::X|FR|rp.point.create.017|                    Enable-ComputerRestore -Drive '%SystemDrive%\', then
::X|FR|rp.point.create.018|                    reg add HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows
::X|FR|rp.point.create.019|                    NT\CurrentVersion\SystemRestore /v
::X|FR|rp.point.create.020|                    SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency /t REG_DWORD /d 0,
::X|FR|rp.point.create.021|                    then Checkpoint-Computer -Description 'OPTY
::X|FR|rp.point.create.022|                    v%current_version% - before optimization'
::X|FR|rp.point.create.023|                    -RestorePointType MODIFY_SETTINGS, then the frequency
::X|FR|rp.point.create.024|                    written back to 1440. Guarded by RP_DONE, so once per
::X|FR|rp.point.create.025|                    session.
::T|EN|rp.point.create.001|SYSTEM RESTORE POINT BEFORE CHANGES
::T|EN|rp.point.create.002|
::T|EN|rp.point.create.003|  What it is      : Before anything destructive runs, OPTY calls
::T|EN|rp.point.create.004|                    :restore_point once per session. It turns System
::T|EN|rp.point.create.005|                    Protection on for the system drive if it was off,
::T|EN|rp.point.create.006|                    briefly sets SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency to 0
::T|EN|rp.point.create.007|                    so Windows cannot refuse a second point inside 24
::T|EN|rp.point.create.008|                    hours, takes one point named after the OPTY version,
::T|EN|rp.point.create.009|                    then writes 1440 back.
::T|EN|rp.point.create.010|
::T|EN|rp.point.create.011|  Actual effect   : A restore point snapshots the registry hives and
::T|EN|rp.point.create.012|                    protected system files through VSS. It does not
::T|EN|rp.point.create.013|                    snapshot your documents, so it is not a backup. The
::T|EN|rp.point.create.014|                    throttle is put back to the Windows default straight
::T|EN|rp.point.create.015|                    afterwards, so OPTY does not leave System Protection
::T|EN|rp.point.create.016|                    permanently altered.
::T|EN|rp.point.create.017|
::T|EN|rp.point.create.018|  Gain            : If a registry write in menu 2 turns out badly on your
::T|EN|rp.point.create.019|                    particular machine, you can roll back from System
::T|EN|rp.point.create.020|                    Restore or from the recovery environment. It is the
::T|EN|rp.point.create.021|                    only undo the script has.
::T|EN|rp.point.create.022|
::T|EN|rp.point.create.023|  Cost            : Shadow-copy storage on C:, typically a few hundred MB
::T|EN|rp.point.create.024|                    to a couple of GB, with Windows deleting the OLDEST
::T|EN|rp.point.create.025|                    point when its quota fills. Plus 10 to 60 seconds. If
::T|EN|rp.point.create.026|                    System Protection was deliberately off, OPTY turns it
::T|EN|rp.point.create.027|                    on and never turns it back off - that part is
::T|EN|rp.point.create.028|                    permanent.
::T|EN|rp.point.create.029|
::T|EN|rp.point.create.030|  Windows default : A clean Windows 11 install ships System Protection OFF
::T|EN|rp.point.create.031|                    for the system drive, and Windows only ever takes
::T|EN|rp.point.create.032|                    points on its own schedule, never on demand. Many OEM
::T|EN|rp.point.create.033|                    images ship it on.
::T|EN|rp.point.create.034|
::T|EN|rp.point.create.035|  Possible values:
::T|EN|rp.point.create.036|    APPLY                : System Protection is switched on for the system
::T|EN|rp.point.create.037|                           drive if it was off, the 24-hour throttle is
::T|EN|rp.point.create.038|                           lifted for the few seconds around the call, one
::T|EN|rp.point.create.039|                           restore point is written, and the throttle is
::T|EN|rp.point.create.040|                           put back to 1440 minutes. Protection stays on
::T|EN|rp.point.create.041|                           afterwards.
::T|EN|rp.point.create.042|    SKIP                 : Nothing is enabled and no point is taken. The
::T|EN|rp.point.create.043|                           machine keeps exactly the System Protection
::T|EN|rp.point.create.044|                           state it had, and the registry writes that
::T|EN|rp.point.create.045|                           follow have no rollback other than a manual
::T|EN|rp.point.create.046|                           undo.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.001|  Why these profiles : Four profiles agree because a safety net does not
::X|EN|rp.point.create.002|                       depend on what the machine is for. The WINDOWS
::X|EN|rp.point.create.003|                       profile is the only one that skips, and for one
::X|EN|rp.point.create.004|                       mechanical reason: enabling System Protection is a
::X|EN|rp.point.create.005|                       persistent configuration change, and that profile
::X|EN|rp.point.create.006|                       exists to leave the shipped state alone. If your
::X|EN|rp.point.create.007|                       image already has protection on, answering yes
::X|EN|rp.point.create.008|                       under any profile costs you a minute and some
::X|EN|rp.point.create.009|                       shadow storage.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.010|
::X|EN|rp.point.create.011|  Unverified      : Whether System Protection ships on or off differs
::X|EN|rp.point.create.012|                    between a clean Windows 11 install and OEM images.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.013|                    OPTY enables it and never turns it back off - only the
::X|EN|rp.point.create.014|                    creation-frequency throttle is restored.
::X|EN|rp.point.create.015|
::X|EN|rp.point.create.016|  Target          : :restore_point, OPTY.bat 3990-4014 - powershell
::X|EN|rp.point.create.017|                    Enable-ComputerRestore -Drive '%SystemDrive%\', then
::X|EN|rp.point.create.018|                    reg add HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows
::X|EN|rp.point.create.019|                    NT\CurrentVersion\SystemRestore /v
::X|EN|rp.point.create.020|                    SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency /t REG_DWORD /d 0,
::X|EN|rp.point.create.021|                    then Checkpoint-Computer -Description 'OPTY
::X|EN|rp.point.create.022|                    v%current_version% - before optimization'
::X|EN|rp.point.create.023|                    -RestorePointType MODIFY_SETTINGS, then the frequency
::X|EN|rp.point.create.024|                    written back to 1440. Guarded by RP_DONE, so once per
::X|EN|rp.point.create.025|                    session.
