:: ---- mo.prefetcher (repair) -------------------------------------
::P|mo.prefetcher|3|3|3|3|3|
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.001|FORCER LE PREFETCH ACTIF (ENABLEPREFETCHER=3)
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.002|
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.003|  Ce que c est    : La valeur 3 active a la fois le prefetch des
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.004|                    applications et celui du demarrage. C'est la meme
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.005|                    ecriture que fait le chemin de restauration, dupliquee
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.006|                    volontairement pour que le chemin SETUP laisse la
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.007|                    machine dans le meme etat connu.
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.008|
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.009|  Effet reel      : Ecrit 3 sans condition, reparant les machines ou un
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.010|                    autre outil avait mis 0 ou 1, et reecrivant le meme
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.011|                    chiffre sur une machine jamais touchee.
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.012|
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.013|  Gain            : Uniquement sur une machine ou un autre outil avait mis
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.014|                    0 ou 1 : l'enregistrement des traces de demarrage et
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.015|                    de lancement reprend, ce qui compte sur un disque
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.016|                    mecanique. Sur un PC SSD sain, aucun gain mesurable -
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.017|                    l'ecriture sert a remettre une machine inconnue dans
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.018|                    un etat connu.
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.019|
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.020|  Cout            : Rien. Quelques Mo de fichiers .pf et un peu d'activite
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.021|                    disque dans les premieres secondes apres le demarrage.
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.022|
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.023|  Defaut Windows  : 3.
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.024|
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.025|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.026|    3                    : Prefetch des applications et prefetch du
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.027|                           demarrage tous deux actifs, ce qu'installe
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.028|                           Windows 11. Les traces de lancement vont dans
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.029|                           les fichiers .pf de C:\Windows\Prefetch, et la
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.030|                           trace de demarrage alimente ReadyBoot.
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.031|    2                    : Demarrage seul. Les traces de lancement
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.032|                           d'applications cessent d'etre rafraichies.
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.033|    1                    : Applications seules. La trace de demarrage
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.034|                           n'est plus entretenue, ReadyBoot perd ses
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.035|                           donnees d'ordonnancement.
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.036|    0                    : Desactive. Ce qu'ecrit le conseil « pas de
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.037|                           prefetch sur SSD ». Cela economise quelques Mo
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.038|                           et un peu d'activite disque dans les premieres
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.039|                           secondes, et aucune mesure ne montre
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.040|                           d'acceleration.
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.041|    absent               : Windows 11 la livre presente a 3 : son absence
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.042|                           signifie qu'un outil l'a retiree et que le
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.043|                           gestionnaire de memoire retombe sur son
::T|FR|mo.prefetcher.044|                           comportement interne.
::X|FR|mo.prefetcher.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq fois 3, pour la meme raison que la fiche du
::X|FR|mo.prefetcher.002|                         chemin de restauration : c'est la valeur Windows
::X|FR|mo.prefetcher.003|                         et le comportement du prefetch ne varie pas selon
::X|FR|mo.prefetcher.004|                         l'usage. Le vieux conseil de couper le prefetch
::X|FR|mo.prefetcher.005|                         sur SSD n'a jamais ete confirme par la mesure.
::X|FR|mo.prefetcher.006|
::X|FR|mo.prefetcher.007|  Cible           : reg add "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\C
::X|FR|mo.prefetcher.008|                    ontrol\Session Manager\Memory
::X|FR|mo.prefetcher.009|                    Management\PrefetchParameters" /v "EnablePrefetcher"
::X|FR|mo.prefetcher.010|                    /t REG_DWORD /d 00000003 /f (OPTY.bat 2157, in
::X|FR|mo.prefetcher.011|                    :map_only). The same write is also performed by
::X|FR|mo.prefetcher.012|                    :reassert_defaults at line 1871.
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.001|ASSERT PREFETCHING ON (ENABLEPREFETCHER=3)
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.002|
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.003|  What it is      : Value 3 enables both application prefetch and boot
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.004|                    prefetch. This is the same write the restore path
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.005|                    makes, deliberately duplicated so the SETUP path
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.006|                    leaves the machine in the same known state.
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.007|
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.008|  Actual effect   : Writes 3 unconditionally, repairing machines where
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.009|                    another tool set 0 or 1, and rewriting the same number
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.010|                    on a machine that was never touched.
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.011|
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.012|  Gain            : Only on a machine where another tool set 0 or 1: boot
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.013|                    and app-launch tracing resume, which matters on a
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.014|                    mechanical disk. On a healthy SSD PC there is no
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.015|                    measurable gain - the point of the write is to put an
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.016|                    unknown machine into a known state.
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.017|
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.018|  Cost            : Nothing. A few MB of .pf files and a little disk
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.019|                    activity in the first seconds after boot.
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.020|
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.021|  Windows default : 3.
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.022|
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.023|  Possible values:
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.024|    3                    : Application prefetching and boot prefetching
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.025|                           both on - what Windows 11 installs. Launch
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.026|                           traces go to .pf files in C:\Windows\Prefetch,
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.027|                           and the boot trace feeds ReadyBoot.
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.028|    2                    : Boot only. Application launch traces stop being
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.029|                           refreshed.
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.030|    1                    : Applications only. The boot trace stops being
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.031|                           maintained, so ReadyBoot loses its ordering
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.032|                           data.
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.033|    0                    : Off. What the 'no prefetch on SSD' advice
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.034|                           writes. It saves a few MB and some first-
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.035|                           seconds disk activity, and no measurement shows
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.036|                           it speeding anything up.
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.037|    absent               : Windows 11 ships it present at 3, so absence
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.038|                           means a tool removed it and the memory manager
::T|EN|mo.prefetcher.039|                           falls back to internal behaviour.
::X|EN|mo.prefetcher.001|  Why these profiles : Five identical threes, for the same reason as the
::X|EN|mo.prefetcher.002|                       restore-path card: this is the Windows value and
::X|EN|mo.prefetcher.003|                       prefetch behaviour does not vary by use case. The
::X|EN|mo.prefetcher.004|                       old advice to disable prefetch on SSDs was never
::X|EN|mo.prefetcher.005|                       supported by measurement.
::X|EN|mo.prefetcher.006|
::X|EN|mo.prefetcher.007|  Target          : reg add "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\C
::X|EN|mo.prefetcher.008|                    ontrol\Session Manager\Memory
::X|EN|mo.prefetcher.009|                    Management\PrefetchParameters" /v "EnablePrefetcher"
::X|EN|mo.prefetcher.010|                    /t REG_DWORD /d 00000003 /f (OPTY.bat 2157, in
::X|EN|mo.prefetcher.011|                    :map_only). The same write is also performed by
::X|EN|mo.prefetcher.012|                    :reassert_defaults at line 1871.
