:: ---- mo.superfetch.killkey (repair) -----------------------------
::P|mo.superfetch.killkey|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.001|SUPPRIMER LA VALEUR HERITEE ENABLESUPERFETCH
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.002|
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.003|  Ce que c est    : Un reliquat de Windows 7 que Windows 11 n'utilise ni
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.004|                    ne cree, loge dans la meme cle PrefetchParameters
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.005|                    qu'EnablePrefetcher.
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.006|
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.007|  Effet reel      : La supprime si elle existe plutot que d'y ecrire une
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.008|                    valeur, puisque toute valeur serait un etat que le
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.009|                    systeme n'a pas.
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.010|
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.011|  Gain            : Aucun effet fonctionnel. Cela evite que la base de
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.012|                    registre affiche un reglage que le systeme n'a plus,
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.013|                    ce qui compte surtout pour la prochaine personne ou le
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.014|                    prochain outil qui la lira.
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.015|
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.016|  Cout            : Rien. Simple remise en ordre.
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.017|
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.018|  Defaut Windows  : Absente.
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.019|
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.020|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.021|    DELETE               : Supprimee si presente, ce qui retablit l'etat
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.022|                           d'origine. Le comportement ne depend alors plus
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.023|                           que du type de demarrage du service SysMain.
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.024|    0                    : L'ancienne valeur « desactive ». L'ecrire sous
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.025|                           Windows 11 cree un etat que le systeme n'a pas
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.026|                           et laisse le registre en desaccord avec la
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.027|                           configuration du service.
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.028|    1, 2 or 3            : Les modes hérités du composant Superfetch de
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.029|                           Vista et Windows 7 - demarrage seul,
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.030|                           applications seules, les deux. Ce composant
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.031|                           n'existe plus sous ce nom.
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.032|    absent               : L'etat Windows 11. Cette cle contient
::T|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.033|                           EnablePrefetcher et rien d'autre.
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq colonnes identiques a DELETE, WINDOWS
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.002|                         compris, parce que l'absence est l'etat livre.
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.003|                         Pour modifier le comportement de SysMain sur
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.004|                         n'importe lequel de ces profils, passez plutot
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.005|                         par le type de demarrage du service.
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.006|
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.007|  Cible           : call :killkey
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.008|                    "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.009|                    Manager\Memory Management\PrefetchParameters"
::X|FR|mo.superfetch.killkey.010|                    "EnableSuperfetch" (OPTY.bat 2158, in :map_only)
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.001|DELETE THE LEGACY ENABLESUPERFETCH VALUE
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.002|
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.003|  What it is      : A leftover from Windows 7 that Windows 11 does not use
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.004|                    or create, sitting in the same PrefetchParameters key
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.005|                    as EnablePrefetcher.
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.006|
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.007|  Actual effect   : Deletes it if present rather than writing a value,
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.008|                    since any value would be a state the OS does not have.
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.009|
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.010|  Gain            : None functional. It stops the registry claiming a
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.011|                    setting the OS no longer has, which matters mostly to
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.012|                    the next person or tool reading it.
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.013|
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.014|  Cost            : Nothing. This is a pure repair.
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.015|
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.016|  Windows default : Absent.
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.017|
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.018|  Possible values:
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.019|    DELETE               : Removed if present, which restores the shipped
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.020|                           state. The behaviour is then decided by the
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.021|                           SysMain service start type alone.
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.022|    0                    : The legacy 'off' value. Writing it on Windows
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.023|                           11 creates a state the OS does not have and
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.024|                           leaves the registry disagreeing with the
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.025|                           service configuration.
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.026|    1, 2 or 3            : The legacy modes from the Vista and Windows 7
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.027|                           Superfetch component - boot only, applications
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.028|                           only, both. That component no longer exists
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.029|                           under this name.
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.030|    absent               : The Windows 11 state. That key holds
::T|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.031|                           EnablePrefetcher and nothing else.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.001|  Why these profiles : Five identical DELETE columns, WINDOWS included,
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.002|                       because absence is the shipped state. To change
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.003|                       SysMain behaviour on any of these profiles, use the
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.004|                       service start type instead.
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.005|
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.006|  Target          : call :killkey
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.007|                    "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session
::X|EN|mo.superfetch.killkey.008|                    Manager\Memory Management\PrefetchParameters"
