:: ---- reg.enableprefetcher (repair) ------------------------------
::P|reg.enableprefetcher|3|3|3|3|3|
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.001|ENABLEPREFETCHER = 3 (VALEUR D'ORIGINE WINDOWS)
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.002|
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.003|  Ce que c est    : Une valeur sous PrefetchParameters qui indique a
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.004|                    Windows quelles traces de prechargement garder : 0 =
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.005|                    rien, 1 = applications, 2 = demarrage, 3 = les deux.
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.006|
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.007|  Effet reel      : Ecrit 3 sans condition. Sur un PC qu'un autre
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.008|                    optimiseur avait mis a 0 ou 1, l'enregistrement des
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.009|                    traces reprend. Sur un PC intact, la meme valeur est
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.010|                    reecrite et rien ne change de visible - et c'est le
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.011|                    but : sur une machine neuve ou inconnue, c'est
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.012|                    l'ecriture qui rend l'etat vrai.
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.013|
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.014|  Gain            : Uniquement sur une machine bidouillee : les traces
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.015|                    reviennent, ce qui joue surtout sur l'ordre de
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.016|                    demarrage via ReadyBoot. Sur un PC SSD sain, aucun
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.017|                    gain mesurable.
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.018|
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.019|  Cout            : Aucun. 3 est la valeur d'usine. Un peu d'activite
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.020|                    disque dans les premieres secondes apres le demarrage,
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.021|                    le temps d'ecrire les traces, et quelques Mo dans
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.022|                    C:\Windows\Prefetch.
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.023|
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.024|  Defaut Windows  : 3 - prechargement des applications et du demarrage,
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.025|                    les deux actifs.
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.026|
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.027|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.028|    3                    : Conserver les deux types de traces : lancements
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.029|                           d'applications et demarrage. Les traces de
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.030|                           lancement sont les fichiers .pf de
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.031|                           C:\Windows\Prefetch ; la trace de demarrage est
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.032|                           consommee par ReadyBoot pour ordonner les
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.033|                           lectures au demarrage.
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.034|    2                    : Traces de demarrage uniquement.
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.035|    1                    : Traces d'applications uniquement.
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.036|    0                    : Aucune trace, et donc aucune lecture anticipee
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.037|                           construite dessus.
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.038|    absent               : Pas un etat livre par Windows 11. La cle
::T|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.039|                           contient normalement cette unique valeur a 3.
::X|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq fois 3. Le prefetch est un comportement du
::X|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.002|                         gestionnaire de memoire, pas une preference de
::X|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.003|                         charge de travail, et la colonne PORTABLE est
::X|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.004|                         identique aux autres parce que la lecture
::X|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.005|                         anticipee tracee remplace des lectures
::X|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.006|                         eparpillees au lieu de s'y ajouter.
::X|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.007|
::X|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.008|  Cible           : EnablePrefetcher under
::X|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.009|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session
::X|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.010|                    Manager\Memory Management\PrefetchParameters, written
::X|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.011|                    as REG_DWORD 3 - OPTY.bat 2157 in :map_only, and again
::X|FR|reg.enableprefetcher.012|                    at line 1871 in :reassert_defaults
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.001|ENABLEPREFETCHER = 3 (WINDOWS DEFAULT)
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.002|
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.003|  What it is      : A value under PrefetchParameters telling Windows which
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.004|                    prefetch traces to keep: 0 = off, 1 = applications, 2
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.005|                    = boot, 3 = both.
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.006|
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.007|  Actual effect   : Writes 3 unconditionally. On a PC another optimizer
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.008|                    set to 0 or 1, boot and app-launch tracing resume. On
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.009|                    an untouched PC the same number is simply rewritten
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.010|                    and nothing observable changes - which is the point:
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.011|                    on a fresh or foreign machine the write is what makes
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.012|                    the state true.
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.013|
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.014|  Gain            : Only on a tweaked machine: traces come back, which
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.015|                    mainly affects boot ordering through ReadyBoot. On a
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.016|                    healthy SSD PC there is no measurable gain.
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.017|
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.018|  Cost            : None. 3 is what Windows ships. A little disk activity
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.019|                    in the first seconds after boot while traces are
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.020|                    written, and a few MB in C:\Windows\Prefetch.
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.021|
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.022|  Windows default : 3 - application prefetching and boot prefetching, both
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.023|                    on.
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.024|
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.025|  Possible values:
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.026|    3                    : Keep both trace kinds: application launches and
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.027|                           boot. The launch traces are the .pf files in
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.028|                           C:\Windows\Prefetch; the boot trace is consumed
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.029|                           by ReadyBoot to order the reads at startup.
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.030|    2                    : Boot traces only.
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.031|    1                    : Application traces only.
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.032|    0                    : No tracing at all, and no read-ahead built from
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.033|                           it.
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.034|    absent               : Not a state Windows 11 ships. The key normally
::T|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.035|                           holds this one value at 3.
::X|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.001|  Why these profiles : Five identical threes. Prefetching is a memory-
::X|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.002|                       manager behaviour, not a workload preference, and
::X|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.003|                       the LAPTOP column matches the rest because the
::X|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.004|                       traced read-ahead replaces scattered reads rather
::X|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.005|                       than adding to them.
::X|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.006|
::X|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.007|  Target          : EnablePrefetcher under
::X|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.008|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session
::X|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.009|                    Manager\Memory Management\PrefetchParameters, written
::X|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.010|                    as REG_DWORD 3 - OPTY.bat 2157 in :map_only, and again
::X|EN|reg.enableprefetcher.011|                    at line 1871 in :reassert_defaults
