:: ---- del.enablesuperfetch (repair) ------------------------------
::P|del.enablesuperfetch|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|DELETE|
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.001|SUPPRIMER LA VALEUR RESIDUELLE ENABLESUPERFETCH
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.002|
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.003|  Ce que c est    : Une valeur de l'epoque Vista et Windows 7 dans la meme
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.004|                    cle PrefetchParameters. Windows 11 ne la cree jamais ;
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.005|                    les guides de bidouille, si, pour tenter de couper
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.006|                    SysMain depuis le registre.
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.007|
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.008|  Effet reel      : La supprime si elle existe, ne fait rien sinon. Le
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.009|                    comportement de SysMain ne depend alors plus que du
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.010|                    type de demarrage du service, et non d'un forcage
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.011|                    perime.
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.012|
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.013|  Gain            : Supprime une contradiction entre « le service dit X,
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.014|                    le registre dit Y ». Si la valeur etait absente, le
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.015|                    gain est nul, litteralement.
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.016|
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.017|  Cout            : Aucun sous Windows 11. Si vous l'aviez posee expres,
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.018|                    passez plutot par le type de demarrage du service :
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.019|                    c'est le reglage que Windows lit a coup sur.
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.020|
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.021|  Defaut Windows  : Valeur absente. Windows 11 ne livre
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.022|                    qu'EnablePrefetcher dans cette cle.
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.023|
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.024|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.025|    DELETE               : La valeur disparait. Rien d'autre ne change :
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.026|                           SysMain garde le type de demarrage qu'il avait,
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.027|                           et ce type de demarrage est le seul reglage que
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.028|                           Windows 11 lit a coup sur pour ce comportement.
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.029|    0                    : La tentative des guides de couper SysMain
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.030|                           depuis le registre. Cela laisse une
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.031|                           contradiction - le service dit une chose, le
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.032|                           registre une autre - sans arreter quoi que ce
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.033|                           soit de facon fiable.
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.034|    1, 2 or 3            : Les modes de Vista et Windows 7. Ils
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.035|                           appartiennent a un composant que Windows 11 ne
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.036|                           configure plus ainsi.
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.037|    absent               : Ce qu'a un Windows 11 propre. Seule
::T|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.038|                           EnablePrefetcher est livree dans cette cle.
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq colonnes identiques a DELETE parce qu'une
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.002|                         valeur que le systeme ne cree pas est fausse sur
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.003|                         tous les profils, WINDOWS le premier. Hesitez
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.004|                         seulement si vous l'avez posee sciemment et savez
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.005|                         ce qui la lit sous Windows 11.
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.006|
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.007|  Non verifie (en)  : Whether any Windows 11 component still reads
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.008|                      EnableSuperfetch is not documented. Deleting it is
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.009|                      safe either way, but do not expect it to change
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.010|                      behaviour.
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.011|
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.012|  Cible           : EnableSuperfetch under
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.013|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.014|                    Manager\Memory Management\PrefetchParameters, removed
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.015|                    by call :killkey - OPTY.bat 2158 in :map_only, and
::X|FR|del.enablesuperfetch.016|                    again at line 1874 in :reassert_defaults
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.001|REMOVE THE LEFTOVER ENABLESUPERFETCH VALUE
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.002|
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.003|  What it is      : A Vista and Windows 7 era value in the same
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.004|                    PrefetchParameters key. Windows 11 never creates it;
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.005|                    tweak guides do, trying to switch SysMain off from the
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.006|                    registry.
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.007|
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.008|  Actual effect   : Deletes it if present, does nothing if absent. SysMain
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.009|                    behaviour is then decided by the service start type
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.010|                    alone, not by a stale override.
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.011|
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.012|  Gain            : Removes one 'the service says X, the registry says Y'
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.013|                    contradiction. If the value was absent, the gain is
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.014|                    literally zero.
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.015|
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.016|  Cost            : None on Windows 11. If you set it on purpose, use the
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.017|                    service start type instead - that is the knob Windows
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.018|                    definitely still reads.
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.019|
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.020|  Windows default : Value absent. Windows 11 ships only EnablePrefetcher
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.021|                    in that key.
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.022|
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.023|  Possible values:
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.024|    DELETE               : The value goes. Nothing else changes: SysMain
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.025|                           keeps whatever start type it had, and that
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.026|                           start type is the only setting Windows 11
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.027|                           definitely reads for this behaviour.
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.028|    0                    : The tweak-guide attempt to switch SysMain off
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.029|                           from the registry. It leaves a contradiction -
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.030|                           the service says one thing, the registry
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.031|                           another - without reliably stopping anything.
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.032|    1, 2 or 3            : The Vista and Windows 7 modes. They belong to a
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.033|                           component that Windows 11 no longer configures
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.034|                           this way.
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.035|    absent               : What a clean Windows 11 has. Only
::T|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.036|                           EnablePrefetcher ships in that key.
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.001|  Why these profiles : Five identical DELETE columns because a value the
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.002|                       OS does not create is wrong on every profile,
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.003|                       WINDOWS most of all. Hesitate only if you placed it
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.004|                       deliberately and can name what reads it on Windows
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.005|                       11.
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.006|
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.007|  Unverified      : Whether any Windows 11 component still reads
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.008|                    EnableSuperfetch is not documented. Deleting it is
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.009|                    safe either way, but do not expect it to change
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.010|                    behaviour.
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.011|
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.012|  Target          : EnableSuperfetch under
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.013|                    HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.014|                    Manager\Memory Management\PrefetchParameters, removed
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.015|                    by call :killkey - OPTY.bat 2158 in :map_only, and
::X|EN|del.enablesuperfetch.016|                    again at line 1874 in :reassert_defaults
