:: ---- rp.checkpoint (preference) -------------------------------------
::P|rp.checkpoint|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|APPLY|
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.001|CREER UN POINT DE RESTAURATION AVANT TOUTE MODIFICATION
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.002|
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.003|  Ce que c est    : Un seul point de restauration systeme, nomme d'apres
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.004|                    la version d'OPTY, pris une fois par session avant
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.005|                    tout changement susceptible de devoir etre annule.
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.006|
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.007|  Effet reel      : Appelle Checkpoint-Computer en type MODIFY_SETTINGS.
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.008|                    Windows prend un instantane des ruches de registre et
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.009|                    des fichiers systeme proteges via VSS. Il ne
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.010|                    sauvegarde pas vos documents et ne l'a jamais fait :
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.011|                    la restauration du systeme n'est pas une sauvegarde.
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.012|                    Si la protection du systeme est coupee, l'appel echoue
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.013|                    simplement et OPTY avertit puis continue.
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.014|
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.015|  Gain            : Un retour en arriere en un clic sur les modifications
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.016|                    de registre et de services, si quelque chose dans
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.017|                    SETUP ou dans la reparation tourne mal sur votre
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.018|                    machine.
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.019|
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.020|  Cout            : Occupe de l'espace de cliches VSS, en general de
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.021|                    quelques centaines de Mo a deux Go. Quand le quota est
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.022|                    plein, Windows supprime silencieusement le point LE
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.023|                    PLUS ANCIEN pour faire de la place : un point plus
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.024|                    vieux sur lequel vous comptiez peut donc disparaitre.
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.025|                    La creation prend 10 a 60 secondes.
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.026|
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.027|  Defaut Windows  : Sans objet - Windows cree des points selon son propre
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.028|                    calendrier, avant l'installation de pilotes et
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.029|                    certaines mises a jour, jamais a la demande.
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.030|
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.031|  Valeurs possibles :
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.032|    APPLY                : Un point de restauration de type
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.033|                           MODIFY_SETTINGS est cree. Le verrou de 1440
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.034|                           minutes est mis a 0 le temps de l'appel puis
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.035|                           reecrit aussitot, pour que Windows ne refuse
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.036|                           pas un point pris moins d'un jour apres un
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.037|                           autre et que la machine ne reste pas modifiee.
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.038|    SKIP                 : Aucun point n'est pris et le verrou n'est
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.039|                           jamais touche. Ce que l'execution modifie n'a
::T|FR|rp.checkpoint.040|                           alors aucune annulation en un clic.
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.001|  Pourquoi ces profils : Cinq colonnes identiques a APPLY, WINDOWS
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.002|                         compris, et voici pourquoi ce profil ne se retire
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.003|                         pas : prendre un point ne modifie aucune
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.004|                         configuration. Le verrou est retabli
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.005|                         immediatement, et si la protection du systeme est
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.006|                         coupee l'appel echoue sans dommage. La seule
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.007|                         raison sensee de refuser : vous relancez OPTY
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.008|                         pour la cinquieme fois de la journee et preferez
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.009|                         garder le point de ce matin plutot que de le
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.010|                         faire sortir du quota.
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.011|
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.012|  Cible           : powershell -NoProfile -Command "Checkpoint-Computer
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.013|                    -Description 'OPTY v%current_version% - before
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.014|                    optimization' -RestorePointType 'MODIFY_SETTINGS'"
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.015|                    (OPTY.bat 4005), framed by
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.016|                    SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency set to 0 at line
::X|FR|rp.checkpoint.017|                    4004 and back to 1440 at line 4013
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.001|CREATE A RESTORE POINT BEFORE CHANGING ANYTHING
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.002|
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.003|  What it is      : A single system restore point, named after the OPTY
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.004|                    version, taken once per session before any change that
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.005|                    might need undoing.
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.006|
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.007|  Actual effect   : Calls Checkpoint-Computer with type MODIFY_SETTINGS.
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.008|                    Windows snapshots the registry hives and protected
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.009|                    system files through VSS. It does not back up your
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.010|                    documents and never has - System Restore is not a
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.011|                    backup. If System Protection is off, the call simply
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.012|                    fails and OPTY warns and continues.
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.013|
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.014|  Gain            : One-click rollback of the registry and service changes
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.015|                    through System Restore if something in SETUP or Repair
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.016|                    turns out badly on your particular machine.
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.017|
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.018|  Cost            : Uses VSS shadow storage, typically a few hundred MB to
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.019|                    a couple of GB. When the shadow quota is full, Windows
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.020|                    silently deletes the OLDEST restore point to make
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.021|                    room, so an older point you were counting on can
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.022|                    disappear. Creation takes roughly 10 to 60 seconds.
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.023|
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.024|  Windows default : Not applicable - Windows creates restore points on its
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.025|                    own schedule, before driver installs and some updates,
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.026|                    never on demand.
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.027|
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.028|  Possible values:
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.029|    APPLY                : One restore point of type MODIFY_SETTINGS is
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.030|                           created. The 1440-minute throttle is set to 0
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.031|                           for the duration of the call and written
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.032|                           straight back afterwards, so Windows does not
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.033|                           refuse a point taken within a day of an earlier
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.034|                           one and the machine is not left permanently
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.035|                           altered.
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.036|    SKIP                 : No point is taken, and the throttle is never
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.037|                           touched. Whatever the run changes has no one-
::T|EN|rp.checkpoint.038|                           click rollback.
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.001|  Why these profiles : Five identical APPLY columns, WINDOWS included, and
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.002|                       here is why that profile does not opt out: taking a
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.003|                       point changes no configuration at all. The throttle
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.004|                       is restored immediately, and if System Protection
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.005|                       is off the call just fails harmlessly. The only
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.006|                       sane reason to decline is that you are re-running
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.007|                       OPTY for the fifth time today and would rather keep
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.008|                       this morning's older point than push it out of the
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.009|                       quota.
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.010|
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.011|  Target          : powershell -NoProfile -Command "Checkpoint-Computer
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.012|                    -Description 'OPTY v%current_version% - before
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.013|                    optimization' -RestorePointType 'MODIFY_SETTINGS'"
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.014|                    (OPTY.bat 4005), framed by
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.015|                    SystemRestorePointCreationFrequency set to 0 at line
::X|EN|rp.checkpoint.016|                    4004 and back to 1440 at line 4013
